(window.__pvQ=window.__pvQ||[]).push({"n":0,"of":1,"total":156,"d":[{"u":"pune/pune-fc-road-pmc-staff-allegedly-found-sleeping-chatting-vehicle.html","h":"FC Road surprise inspection: PMC staff allegedly found sleeping, chatting in vehicle during duty","s":"BJP corporator Ravi Satgaonkar, who made a surprise inspection of FC Road, has questioned the lack of effective enforcement and wants civic staff monitored more strictly.","k":"FC Road","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-14T13:08:25+05:30","g":["FC Road","PMC","Encroachments","Ravi Satgaonkar","Pune"],"b":"Pune Municipal Corporation (PMC) staff were allegedly found sleeping and chatting inside a vehicle on FC Road during duty, instead of carrying out their assigned duties, in a surprise inspection by BJP corporator Ravi Satgaonkar.\nThe inspection has raised questions about how the PMC's anti-encroachment department works.\nIt also brought up concerns over illegal roadside stalls, hawkers and encroachments that affect pedestrians and traffic on the road.\nSatgaonkar questioned the lack of effective enforcement and called for stricter monitoring of civic staff so that action against encroachments is taken regularly.","i":"illustration-1b36ee61e4","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pune-pmc-commissioner-bars-central-funds-transfer-to-wards-amid-diversion-row.html","h":"PMC Commissioner bars transfer of central funds to wards amid fund diversion row","s":"A Pune Municipal Corporation circular bars central departments from moving funds to ward works but does not clarify the status of transfers the standing committee has already approved.","k":"PMC funds","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-14T12:57:22+05:30","g":["PMC","Naval Kishore Ram","Fund diversion","Standing committee"],"b":"PMC Commissioner Naval Kishore Ram bars central departments from making their budgetary allocations available for ward office works without following the prescribed financial provisions, amid a row over a standing committee resolution to divert funds.\nIn the circular, the commissioner said such transfers were not appropriate from the perspective of financial planning. The commissioner directed all central departments of the Pune Municipal Corporation not to make their budgetary allocations available for works under ward offices without following the prescribed financial provisions.\nThe row concerns a standing committee resolution to divert around Rs 5.5 crore, earmarked in the budget for development works in the Kasewadi-Dias Plot area of ward 22, to ward 23-D. BJP corporators have opposed the move. Congress corporator Rafiq Shaikh has sought its cancellation, alleging that the funds were diverted without taking the elected representatives concerned into confidence.\nA similar controversy has emerged over diverting around Rs 5.5 crore, reserved for two development works in the Bund Garden area, to road works in the Taljai area.\nThe circular does not clarify the status of fund transfers already approved by the standing committee.","i":"","a":[]},{"u":"pune/moshi-deaf-mute-men-tied-up-beaten-on-suspicion-of-kidnapping-children.html","h":"Child-lifting rumour: two deaf-mute men tied up, beaten in Moshi","s":"Two deaf-mute men tied up and beaten in Moshi on suspicion of kidnapping children had only come to a housing society to ask for donations, a police inquiry found.","k":"Moshi","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-14T12:46:44+05:30","g":["Moshi","Pimpri-Chinchwad","Shivajiwadi","Dial 112"],"b":"As per the police, local residents caught two deaf-mute men at Shivajiwadi in Moshi, Pimpri-Chinchwad, on suspicion of kidnapping children, a child-lifting rumour, and tied them up with rope; the men were also beaten.\nOn 13 November the Moshi marshals received a Dial 112 call saying locals had held two men at Shivajiwadi, within Moshi village limits, on suspicion of kidnapping children. Police rushed to the spot.\nThe police inquiry found that the two men had come to a housing society only to ask for donations, and no attempt to kidnap children, or any other wrongdoing, was found.\nA non-cognisable offence has been registered against two people for beating the two men.","i":"","a":["Moshi"]},{"u":"pune/deccan-banner-asks-who-is-protecting-those-behind-ajit-pawar-plane-crash.html","h":"Deccan bus stand banner asks who is protecting those behind Ajit Pawar’s plane crash","s":"A banner in Pune that announces a programme at the Yashwantrao Chavan Centre in Mumbai on 16 November 2026 has raised questions about who is behind the campaign.","k":"Deccan banner","c":"Politics","t":"2026-11-14T11:59:54+05:30","g":["Ajit Pawar","Deccan bus stand","Plane crash","Banner"],"b":"Near Deccan bus stand in Pune, a banner asks who is protecting those behind the late Ajit Pawar’s plane crash and announces a programme on 16 November 2026 at 4 pm at the Yashwantrao Chavan Centre in Mumbai.\nThe banner questions the circumstances of the late Ajit Pawar’s plane crash and asks: “Who is the leader protecting those behind Ajit Dada’s accident or alleged sabotage?”\nIt has drawn attention and raised questions about who is behind the campaign and what the organisers intend to reveal.","i":"","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pune-voters-say-addresses-shifted-without-knowledge-ncp-complaint.html","h":"Pune voters say addresses were shifted without their knowledge, NCP leader's complaint lists 58 names","s":"Of 58 names on an NCP leader's complaint list, three voters had died and 11 were living where they were registered, the Pune District Election Officer found.","k":"Voter addresses","c":"Politics","t":"2026-11-14T11:49:18+05:30","g":["Pune voters","Ajit Gavhane","Form 8","Bhosari","Nigdi Police Station"],"b":"Voters in Pune say their addresses were shifted to other constituencies without their knowledge; NCP leader Ajit Gavhane hand-delivered a complaint with a list of 58 names on November 19, 2025, claiming “fraudulent deletions/ shifting of voters” and more than 15,000 cases.\nAt least six of the voters on the list said they had neither shifted residences nor submitted any form to change their address. One said her voter address was shifted to Ovala Majiwada in Thane without her knowledge.\nIn their reports, election officials in Pimpri, Thane and Khadakvasla admitted that Form 8 address change requests had been approved without any field check by Booth Level Officers. The Pune District Election Officer issued a show cause notice to the Pimpri Electoral Registration Officer.\nOn November 1, the Pimpri Assistant ERO filed a non-cognizable offence report at Nigdi Police Station under Section 31 of the Representation of the People Act, 1950, against persons who used four mobile numbers to file 40 Form 8 applications.\nThe Pune District Election Officer found that, of the 58 voters, three had died and 11 were living where they were registered. Form 6 applications have since been filed to bring the remaining 43 back on the rolls in Bhosari Assembly constituency.\nMaharashtra Chief Electoral Officer S Chockalingam said the issue of bulk filing had now been addressed by making an Aadhaar-based digital signature mandatory, introduced by the Election Commission in September 2025.","i":"illustration-a0f45732cf","a":["Bhosari"]},{"u":"pune/pune-nagpur-luxury-bus-plunges-off-flyover-woman-killed.html","h":"Chhatrapati Sambhajinagar: Pune–Nagpur luxury bus plunges off flyover, woman killed, over 20 injured","s":"A Pune–Nagpur luxury bus plunged off a flyover in Chhatrapati Sambhajinagar, killing a woman and injuring over 20 passengers, and local residents began rescue operations.","k":"Chhatrapati Sambhajinagar","c":"Accidents and fires","t":"2026-11-14T11:38:43+05:30","g":["Pune–Nagpur luxury bus","Chhatrapati Sambhajinagar","flyover","Cambridge Chowk"],"b":"A woman was killed and more than 20 passengers were seriously injured when a private luxury bus travelling from Pune to Nagpur plunged off a flyover near Cambridge Chowk in Chhatrapati Sambhajinagar on Saturday morning.\nThe driver allegedly lost control of the speeding bus while crossing the flyover. The bus crashed through the protective railing and fell onto the road below.\nSeveral passengers were asleep at the time, according to preliminary information. Several were trapped inside the badly damaged vehicle.\nBefore the police arrived, local residents began rescue operations, breaking the glass panes of the bus windows to get the injured out.\nPolice officials said the injured had been admitted to nearby hospitals and that the condition of some passengers was critical.","i":"illustration-d4ce65c59e","a":[]},{"u":"pune/sinhgad-trust-maruti-navale-reports-deccan-police-station-pune-court-order.html","h":"Sinhgad Trust’s Maruti Navale reports at Deccan police station in Pune with wife, daughter, under court order","s":"Sinhgad Trust trustees, including Maruti Navale, face a ban on leaving Pune city limits in connection with employees’ pending salaries.","k":"Sinhgad Trust","c":"Courts","t":"2026-11-14T11:26:37+05:30","g":["Sinhgad Trust","Maruti Navale","Bombay High Court","Pune"],"b":"A Bombay High Court order requires Sinhgad Trust’s Maruti Navale to report to Deccan Police Station in Pune, and on Friday he did so, accompanied by his wife and daughter.\nNavale must report to the police station each Friday, between 6 pm and 7 pm. On November 10, the High Court imposed restrictions on him and other trustees, including a ban on leaving Pune city limits and an order to deposit their passports with the court.\nThe restrictions relate to the pending salaries of Sinhgad Trust employees. The trust had promised ₹60.65 crore in outstanding salaries, but did not fulfil that commitment.\nThe CBI, the Enforcement Directorate and the Income Tax Department have also been directed by the court to examine the trust’s financial transactions.","i":"","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pune-fake-website-promising-liquor-home-delivery-dupes-customers.html","h":"Pune: Fake website promising liquor home delivery dupes customers","s":"Police have launched an investigation into a fake website that promised home delivery of alcohol in Pune, and a case has been registered against unidentified persons.","k":"Yerawada","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-14T11:16:01+05:30","g":["Pune","Yerawada","Fake website","Yerawada police"],"b":"Fraudsters allegedly used a fake website promising home delivery of alcohol in Pune to cheat the owner of a liquor shop in Yerawada of over ₹1 lakh. According to his complaint, the incident was reported between August and November 2026.\nThe owner filed a complaint at Yerawada police station on Thursday. The fraudsters allegedly created the website in the shop's name.\nThe website carried the fraudsters' own QR code and contact numbers, through which they accepted money and duped several customers. The owner realised the fraud when customers complained that alcohol was not delivered despite payment.\nA case has been registered against unidentified persons. Police have launched an investigation to identify those behind the fake website and trace the money transferred by the victims.","i":"illustration-32f6efeb9e","a":["Yerawada","Yerwada","Yeravda","Yerawda","Yerwda"]},{"u":"pune/pune-fda-suspends-licences-vaishali-roopali-fc-road-food-safety.html","h":"FDA suspends licences of popular Hotel Vaishali, Roopali Restaurant on FC Road over food safety violations","s":"Hotel Vaishali and Roopali Restaurant on FC Road may not run any food business activity, home delivery, parcel services, takeaway and food sales included, until further orders.","k":"FC Road","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-14T11:05:24+05:30","g":["FDA","FC Road","Food safety","Hotel Vaishali","Roopali Restaurant"],"b":"Hotel Vaishali and Roopali Restaurant, two popular and well-known restaurants on Fergusson College (FC) Road, have had their food business licences suspended with immediate effect by the Food and Drug Administration (FDA), Maharashtra, after inspections on November 13, 2026 revealed serious violations of food safety and hygiene standards.\nAssistant Commissioner (Food) Syed Imran Hashmi ordered the suspensions. The action was taken under the FDA’s Safe Food, Safe Maharashtra campaign.\nHotel Vaishali, at 1218, FC Road, Shivajinagar, scored 58 out of 98, which resulted in a ‘Non-Compliance’ classification. Officials said a freezer used for storing raw materials was placed immediately next to the women’s washroom and the griddle for dosa and uttappa was next to the men’s washroom. Officials said boiled potatoes, cooked rice and other prepared food were stored in an open corridor.\nThe restaurant had been inspected in June 2026 and issued a notice to rectify the deficiencies, but serious violations were found again.\nOfficials said the kitchen at Roopali Restaurant, at 1227/2, FC Road, Shivajinagar, was open and inadequately protected, exposing food preparation areas to dust, dirt and insects. They also found stagnant water on the premises, and food stored without proper covering, labelling or ‘Use By’ dates.\nBoth establishments are barred from any food business activity, including food sales, takeaway, parcel services and home delivery, until further orders. They can resume only after rectifying all major deficiencies, complying with food safety standards during a fresh inspection and obtaining written permission from the FDA.","i":"illustration-cf6ec4577d","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pune-airport-eatery-temporarily-shut-after-video-shows-cockroach.html","h":"Pune airport eatery temporarily shut after video shows cockroach crawling among food","s":"A Pune airport eatery will reopen only if it clears an inspection, and Balaji Caterers has imposed a hefty penalty on the eatery's brand.","k":"Pune airport","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-14T10:37:35+05:30","g":["Pune airport","Balaji Caterers","Santosh Dhoke","Hygiene"],"b":"A Pune airport eatery inside the terminal is temporarily shut, and Balaji Caterers has suspended its operations with immediate effect, after a video that shows a cockroach crawling among food items in its display case surfaced on social media.\nBalaji Caterers, the master concessionaire managing all airport food outlets, closed the popular cafe, Pune Airport director Santosh Dhoke said. It also imposed a hefty penalty on the brand and ordered deep cleaning and pest-control measures.\nThe video was shared widely online. The post that shared it tagged state FDA commissioner Tukaram Mundhe and alleged poor hygiene at the outlet and its other branches. The date of the incident remains unclear.\nThe eatery will undergo an internal audit and will reopen only if it clears the inspection. “There can be no compromise on hygiene and food quality at airport food outlets,” Dhoke said.\nPune airport has around 16 food outlets inside the terminal. All outlets would now face tighter scrutiny, airport sources have said.","i":"","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pune-study-indian-diet-encouraging-results-early-type-2-diabetes.html","h":"Pune study: Indian diet shows encouraging results in early Type 2 diabetes","s":"A Pune study of 87 adults with early Type 2 diabetes recorded remission without glucose-lowering medication in 53 participants at the end of six months.","k":"Pune study","c":"City","t":"2026-11-14T00:43:30+05:30","g":["Pune","Type 2 diabetes","Indian diet","Diabetes remission"],"b":"A study by Chellaram Diabetes Institute, Pune, and Dr Kale’s Diabetes and Psychiatry Clinic, Chhatrapati Sambhajinagar, shows encouraging results from a six-month Indian diet and exercise plan in early Type 2 diabetes: 60.9% of adults reached remission.\nThe study involved 87 adults who had had diabetes for up to two years. It was published in the journal Diabetes and Metabolic Syndrome: Clinical Research and Reviews (Elsevier, 2026).\nParticipants followed a Local Healthy Moderate Carbohydrate (LHMC) diet of familiar Indian foods such as multigrain chapatis, lentils, sprouts, green leafy vegetables, nuts and fruits, in defined portions. The plan also included 40 minutes of daily walking and 10 minutes of deep breathing exercises.\nAt the end of six months, 53 participants (60.9%) achieved remission without glucose-lowering medication. Average weight fell by 4.67 kg, and average HbA1c fell from 7.32% to 6.27%. Those who followed the walking routine on at least 80% of days had 8.24 times higher adjusted odds of remission than those with lower adherence.\nDr A G Unnikrishnan, CEO and Endocrinologist, Chellaram Hospital Diabetes Care and Multispecialty, said a larger controlled trial must now confirm the findings, and that patients should change their treatment only in consultation with their doctor.","i":"illustration-80126ac779","a":[]},{"u":"pune/milk-to-cost-4-more-per-litre-in-maharashtra-from-november-16.html","h":"Milk to cost ₹4 more per litre in Maharashtra from November 16","s":"Dairy product prices will rise by up to 10%, the Milk Producers and Processors Welfare Association decided at a meeting of its members on Friday, November 13.","k":"Milk prices","c":"Business","t":"2026-11-14T00:32:55+05:30","g":["Milk prices","Maharashtra","Katraj Dairy","Pune"],"b":"Cow and buffalo milk will cost ₹4 more per litre in Maharashtra from Monday, November 16, the Milk Producers and Processors Welfare Association has decided.\nThe association has also decided to raise the prices of dairy products by up to 10%. Its members took the decision at a meeting on Friday, November 13, at the Pune District Cooperative Milk Producers' Union Limited (Katraj Dairy) in Katraj, Pune, chaired by association president Gopalrao Mhaske.\nKatraj Dairy Chairman Arun Chambhare, association Honorary Secretary Prakash Kutwal and around 50 representatives of major cooperative and private dairy organisations from across Maharashtra attended the meeting.\nAccording to the association, higher diesel prices, transportation charges, sugar prices, packaging material costs and labour expenses have put additional financial pressure on milk processing and distribution businesses, and the procurement prices paid to milk producers have also increased. The association said procurement prices could rise further in the coming months.","i":"illustration-6518375c60","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pune-airport-fine-vehicles-overstaying-15-minute-limit-december.html","h":"Pune airport: ₹500 fine for vehicles overstaying 15-minute pick-up, drop-off limit from December","s":"Vehicles overstaying the 15-minute pick-up and drop-off limit at Pune airport will not be fined during a month-long awareness campaign that continues until November 30.","k":"Pune airport","c":"City","t":"2026-11-14T00:22:24+05:30","g":["Pune airport","Time limit","Boom barrier","ANPR cameras"],"b":"From December, vehicles overstaying the 15-minute limit at pick-up and drop-off at Pune airport will have to pay ₹500, and the exit boom barrier will remain closed until the penalty is paid.\nThe penalty will be imposed after a month-long awareness campaign, which is underway and will continue until November 30. No fines will be levied during this period. AeroMall authorities are enforcing a stricter time-bound entry system to prevent congestion near the terminal.\nThe time limit will be monitored through automatic number plate recognition (ANPR) cameras that record each vehicle's registration number at entry and its exit time. AeroMall also plans to install two display screens near the departure area to show each vehicle's registration number and remaining time.\nY S Rajput, vice-president of AeroMall, said the decision was taken to stop vehicles waiting for long periods near the terminal, particularly during evening peak hours. Around 12,000 to 14,000 cars enter the airport premises every day on average, he said.\nRajput said the restriction is in line with similar systems at major airports, including Delhi. Government officials' vehicles would also be made aware of the new system, he said, though certain VVIP movements are governed by security protocols handled by state authorities and the police.","i":"illustration-d209b4e286","a":[]},{"u":"pune/over-200-stranded-spicejet-cancels-pune-patna-flight-after-hours-of-delay.html","h":"Over 200 stranded as SpiceJet cancels Pune-Patna flight after hours of delay","s":"Passengers on SpiceJet's cancelled Pune-Patna flight allege they got no clear updates, refreshments or adequate assistance during a wait of nearly 10 to 12 hours.","k":"Pune airport","c":"City","t":"2026-11-14T00:11:50+05:30","g":["Pune airport","Pune-Patna flight","Chhath Puja"],"b":"SpiceJet cancelled its 8.20 pm Pune-Patna flight after hours of delay, leaving over 200 people stranded at Pune airport on Thursday night.\nPassengers said they were first told the flight had been rescheduled to 11.25 pm, then to 12.45 am. They said they were repeatedly told it would leave in 10 or 15 minutes, even after the cabin crew had boarded.\nPassengers alleged that they waited for nearly 10 to 12 hours without clear updates, refreshments or adequate assistance. Passengers also alleged that they found out about the cancellation only by checking the flight status online, without any formal communication from the airline.\nAngry passengers staged a protest near the airport's entry gate, demanding accountability and alternative travel arrangements. Families heading to Bihar for Chhath Puja were left distressed by the cancellation, and some passengers were forced to make their own travel arrangements at considerably higher fares.\nPassengers also complained of inadequate seating near the boarding gates, with elderly people and families with children standing for hours. Airport authority personnel later arranged vada pav, but passengers said the quantity was insufficient.\nPassengers alleged they were told refunds could take around seven days. SpiceJet has not commented on the allegations or the cancellation.","i":"","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pune-police-recover-jewellery-cash-uttar-pradesh-after-25-day-hunt.html","h":"Pune Police recover ₹26.33 lakh in jewellery, cash from Uttar Pradesh after 25-day hunt","s":"Over 25 days a police team made three trips to Uttar Pradesh, covering more than 10,000 kilometres, in the investigation into the alleged embezzlement of a bag containing jewellery and ₹28 lakh in cash.","k":"Khadak Police","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-14T00:01:16+05:30","g":["Khadak Police","Pune Police","Uttar Pradesh","Alleged embezzlement"],"b":"Jewellery and cash worth ₹26.33 lakh were recovered from Uttar Pradesh by Khadak Police after a 25-day hunt, an investigation into the alleged embezzlement of a bag containing jewellery and ₹28 lakh in cash.\nThe complainant had entrusted the bag to his 20-year-old employee to deposit at an office in Mumbai. The employee allegedly got off midway and fled without delivering it.\nInvestigators found that the employee's brother and three associates had allegedly conspired in the offence.\nThe police team travelled more than 10,000 kilometres over 25 days, making three trips to Uttar Pradesh. Technical analysis and informants helped trace the suspects in Uttar Pradesh and Uttarakhand. With the help of local police, they were taken into custody in Etah, Kasganj and Gautam Buddha Nagar districts.\nTwo gold biscuits weighing 120 grams, valued at ₹16.80 lakh, were recovered from one associate's home. Another associate, identified as the brother's brother-in-law, was traced at the brother's in-laws' home and arrested for allegedly assisting in the offence. ₹7 lakh in cash, a gold ring and a silver chain were recovered from his home.\nThe suspects allegedly confessed to the offence, police said.\nA case was registered at Khadak Police Station under Section 316(4) of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita. Deputy Commissioner of Police (Zone 1) Krushikesh Rawale gave the details. The operation was conducted under the guidance of Police Commissioner Amitesh Kumar.","i":"","a":[]},{"u":"pune/chakan-midc-aaditya-thackeray-asks-if-1400-crore-package-released.html","h":"Chakan MIDC: Aaditya Thackeray asks if ₹1,400 crore package has been released","s":"On Aaditya Thackeray's second visit to Chakan MIDC in three months, the Shiv Sena (UBT) MLA claimed that irregular water supply, traffic congestion and pothole-ridden roads remained unresolved.","k":"Chakan MIDC","c":"Politics","t":"2026-11-13T20:40:03+05:30","g":["Aaditya Thackeray","Chakan MIDC","Shiv Sena (UBT)","Infrastructure"],"b":"Shiv Sena (UBT) MLA Aaditya Thackeray questioned the Maharashtra government on Friday over whether the ₹1,400 crore infrastructure package for Chakan MIDC, to which Chief Minister Devendra Fadnavis gave in-principle approval in September, has been released.\n“The Chief Minister had announced ₹1,400 crore. Has that money arrived? Have they released it? This question still remains,” Thackeray said.\nOn his second visit to Chakan MIDC in three months, Thackeray claimed that pothole-ridden roads, traffic congestion, garbage management, irregular water supply and electricity issues remained unresolved. The only visible change since August, he said, was that regular meetings had started between the district administration and other stakeholders.\nThackeray demanded that the administration make its progress report public.\nAround 20 industrial units in Chakan had considered relocating to Khandala MIDC in Satara district in August. The Chakan Industrial Association later said the companies had dropped their immediate relocation plans following government assurances.\n“If this is the situation in Chakan, Hinjawadi and several other MIDCs, which industrialists will want to come to Maharashtra?” Thackeray asked.\nThackeray suggested mill-and-fill resurfacing for damaged asphalt roads, claiming several roads could be repaired within four days. He also said farmers must receive the compensation due to them for land acquired for infrastructure projects.","i":"","a":["Chakan"]},{"u":"pune/loni-kalbhor-hotel-assault-former-sarpanch-among-four-booked-online-payment-row.html","h":"Loni Kalbhor hotel assault: former sarpanch among four booked after online food payment row","s":"Loni Kalbhor police have registered a case against four accused men, one of them a former sarpanch, over an alleged assault at a hotel.","k":"Loni Kalbhor hotel assault","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-13T19:49:22+05:30","g":["Loni Kalbhor","Former sarpanch","Assault","Jagdamba Hotel"],"b":"A dispute over an online food payment at Jagdamba Hotel in Loni Kalbhor turned violent on November 9: four men, including a former sarpanch, allegedly assaulted the hotel owner, his son and a customer.\nLoni Kalbhor police have registered a case against the four accused.","i":"illustration-60abbaebd2","a":["Loni Kalbhor"]},{"u":"pune/pune-sinhgad-society-major-action-administrators-run-32-colleges.html","h":"Major action on Pune's Sinhgad society: administrators run 32 colleges after Bombay High Court orders","s":"Seven Sinhgad Technical Education Society colleges under the Directorate of Higher Education now have administrators appointed for three years, and the Directorate of Technical Education has appointed administrators for 25 more by an order that took effect immediately.","k":"Sinhgad colleges","c":"City","t":"2026-11-13T19:38:42+05:30","g":["Sinhgad Technical Education Society","Bombay High Court","Higher Education","Pune"],"b":"The state's Directorate of Higher Education and Directorate of Technical Education have put 32 colleges of Pune's Sinhgad Technical Education Society under administrators, against the backdrop of the Bombay High Court's order on petitions filed over employees' salaries. This is a major action: the administrators now run the colleges.\nAdministrators have been appointed for three years to seven colleges under the Directorate of Higher Education, under section 3(1) of the Maharashtra Educational Institutions (Management) Act, 1976. The Joint Director of Higher Education, Pune division, is the administrator.\nThe Directorate of Technical Education has appointed administrators for 25 colleges, with the Joint Director at its Pune regional office in charge. That order took effect immediately. The 25 include engineering, technology, hotel management, pharmacy and diploma colleges.\nThe seven colleges: Sinhgad Law College, Ambegaon; Shrimati Kashibai Navale College of Education, Kusgaon; Sinhgad Arts and Commerce College, Narhe; Nivrutti Babaji Navale Commerce and Science College, Kusgaon; Sinhgad Commerce College, Kondhwa; Shrimati Kashibai Navale Commerce College, Erandwane; and Sinhgad Science College, Ambegaon.\nThe administrators are now responsible for resolving the management's problems, keeping the colleges running and protecting students' academic interests.\nSalaries of the society's teaching and non-teaching staff are alleged to have gone unpaid for years, and employees had protested over it. A petition brought to the High Court's notice that more than 13 employees had died by suicide amid the financial distress. The court directed action as per law.\nHigher Education Director Dr Shailendra Deolankar and Technical Education Director Dr Pramod Naik issued separate circulars. Dr Deolankar said the decision was taken in the public interest in the light of the court's order.","i":"illustration-d040abdabf","a":[]},{"u":"pune/mohammadwadi-acropolis-purple-tribeca-raheja-vistas-revenue-department-scanner.html","h":"Mohammadwadi: Acropolis, Purple, Tribeca, Elina Living, Raheja Vistas under Revenue Department scanner","s":"Acting on directions from Pune District Collector Jitendra Dudi, a Deputy Collector has begun further legal and penal proceedings over properties affected in the Mohammadwadi land transactions under scrutiny.","k":"Mohammadwadi","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-13T19:27:57+05:30","g":["Mohammadwadi","Revenue Department","Acropolis","Raheja Vistas"],"b":"Acropolis, Purple, Tribeca, The Ark, Elina Living and Raheja Vistas are among the major real estate developments in Pune’s Mohammadwadi area now under the Revenue Department’s scanner. Alleged violations of land transfer conditions were detected in transactions involving Survey Numbers 44 and 38/1C, and these are among the projects identified in connection with the land transactions under scrutiny.\nAccording to the Revenue Department, scrutiny of land records revealed that certain properties were transferred without prior permission from the competent authority, allegedly in violation of conditions under Section 43 of the Bombay Tenancy and Agricultural Lands Act, 1948.\nThe findings raise questions over whether developers met mandatory legal requirements before starting residential and commercial projects worth crores of rupees.\nThe Deputy Collector (Revenue, Tenancy Act Branch), acting on directions from Pune District Collector Jitendra Dudi, issued a communication dated October 31, 2026, initiating further legal and penal proceedings concerning the affected properties.\nThe complainant in the matter speaks in the video on the Instagram post.","i":"","a":["Mohammadwadi","Mohamadwadi","Mohammedwadi"]},{"u":"pune/pune-resident-threatens-dump-sewage-pcmc-bungalow-leak-near-pimpri-station.html","h":"‘Will dump this sewage in PCMC Commissioner’s bungalow’: resident over leak near Pimpri Railway Station","s":"A resident has alleged that sewage leaking from a toilet chamber near Pimpri Railway Station risks health hazards for commuters and people living nearby.","k":"Pimpri Railway Station","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-13T18:30:41+05:30","g":["Pimpri Railway Station","PCMC","Sewage leak","Sanitation"],"b":"Frustrated over the alleged lack of action, a resident has threatened to collect sewage that leaks from a toilet chamber near Pimpri Railway Station and dump it in the bungalow of the Pimpri-Chinchwad Municipal Corporation (PCMC) Commissioner, if the problem remains unresolved.\nHe has alleged that the leak is creating unhygienic conditions in the area, raising the risk of health hazards for commuters and people living nearby.\nHe also questioned how Pimpri-Chinchwad secured the distinction of being Maharashtra’s cleanest city despite such sanitation issues.","i":"","a":["Pimpri","Pimpri Camp","Pimpri Gaon"]},{"u":"pune/gayatri-barua-wife-of-jahnu-barua-dies-suspected-cardiac-arrest-pune.html","h":"Jahnu Barua’s wife Gayatri dies of suspected cardiac arrest in Pune","s":"Doctors declared Gayatri Barua, wife of filmmaker Jahnu Barua, dead at a nearby hospital after she collapsed during a meal at a city restaurant.","k":"Pune","c":"City","t":"2026-11-13T17:32:44+05:30","g":["Gayatri Barua","Jahnu Barua","NFAI","Pune"],"b":"Gayatri Barua, wife of noted filmmaker Jahnu Barua, collapsed while having a meal at a city restaurant on Thursday, November 12, and died in Pune after a suspected cardiac arrest.\nThe couple was in Pune to view the restoration of Jahnu Barua’s films at the National Film Archive of India (NFAI). The collapse came after visiting the archive.\nShe was rushed to a nearby hospital, where doctors examined her and declared her dead.","i":"illustration-bb7e6d474c","a":[]},{"u":"pune/major-fire-breaks-out-at-mhetrewasti-plastic-factory-pimpri-chinchwad.html","h":"Major fire at plastic factory in Mhetrewasti, Pimpri-Chinchwad","s":"A fire at a plastic factory in Mhetrewasti was brought under control in time by fire brigade personnel, and its cause is yet to be established.","k":"Fire at Mhetrewasti","c":"Accidents and fires","t":"2026-11-13T17:21:40+05:30","g":["Mhetrewasti fire","Pimpri-Chinchwad","Plastic factory fire","Pune"],"b":"A major fire broke out at around 3:45 pm at a plastic injection manufacturing company in the Chinchacha Mala area of Mhetrewasti, Pimpri-Chinchwad.\nFire brigade personnel rushed to the spot and brought the blaze under control in time. No casualties were reported.\nA large quantity of materials inside the factory is said to have been damaged. The cause of the fire is yet to be established.","i":"","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pune-metro-start-services-15-november-national-unity-run-soldierathon.html","h":"Pune Metro to start services on 15 November for National Unity Run, Soldierathon participants","s":"Pune Metro will run trains every 20 minutes on both corridors between 3.40 am and 6 am for National Unity Run and Soldierathon participants.","k":"Pune Metro","c":"City","t":"2026-11-13T16:57:59+05:30","g":["Pune Metro","National Unity Run","Soldierathon"],"b":"The first Pune Metro trains for National Unity Run and Soldierathon participants will leave Ramwadi, Vanaz, PCMC and Swargate stations. Services will start at 3.40 am on 15 November.\nBetween 3.40 am and 6 am, trains will run every 20 minutes on both corridors, and additional services every 10 minutes from the District Court interchange towards Vanaz and PCMC.\nSoldierathon runners can take the PCMC corridor, while participants heading to Alka Chowk can use the Vanaz corridor.\nPune Metro authorities have urged participants to use public transport.","i":"illustration-3fef41cf50","a":[]},{"u":"pune/solapur-airport-training-aircraft-from-baramati-hard-lands-pilot-safe.html","h":"Solapur airport: training aircraft from Baramati hard-lands, pilot safe","s":"Solapur airport director Anjani Kumari said the Redbird Flying Training Academy aircraft that hard-landed there can be removed only once a Directorate General of Civil Aviation (DGCA) team has inspected it and given clearance.","k":"Solapur airport","c":"Accidents and fires","t":"2026-11-13T16:21:32+05:30","g":["Solapur airport","Baramati","DGCA","training aircraft","hard landing"],"b":"A training aircraft of Redbird Flying Training Academy made a hard landing at Solapur airport around 2 pm on Thursday; the trainee pilot is safe.\nThe single-engine, twin-seater Tecnam P-Mentor had taken off from Baramati, where the academy is based, around 1.15 pm, with a trainee pilot who has 160 hours of flying on board.\nThe landing damaged the nose wheel, which broke and bent. Its front portion came into contact with the runway, and the aircraft came to rest on its front body, stranded on the runway. Its front tyre burst.\nAn academy spokesperson said the trainee pilot had not sustained any injuries.\nSolapur airport director Anjani Kumari said the aircraft did not veer off the runway. It can be removed only after a Directorate General of Civil Aviation (DGCA) team inspects it and gives clearance, she said. There are no scheduled aircraft movements at Solapur for now, she said.\nThis comes amid a series of mishaps involving training aircraft in and around Baramati. In August, a Carver Aviation training aircraft veered off the table-top runway at the Baramati airstrip; both occupants escaped unhurt.","i":"","a":["Baramati","Baramati city","Baramati taluka"]},{"u":"pune/pune-woman-sugarcane-worker-dies-several-injured-tractor-trolley-overturns-murti.html","h":"Woman sugarcane worker dies, several injured when tractor trolley overturns near Murti in Baramati taluka","s":"A tractor trolley carrying sugarcane workers overturned near Murti in Baramati taluka, killing one woman worker and seriously injuring other workers.","k":"Baramati taluka","c":"Accidents and fires","t":"2026-11-13T16:10:59+05:30","g":["Baramati taluka","Murti","Sugarcane workers","Tractor trolley"],"b":"A woman sugarcane worker died and several were injured when a tractor trolley carrying about 15 to 20 sugarcane workers overturned near Murti in Baramati taluka at around 5 o'clock on Thursday, 12 November.\nTwo tractors were taking the workers to the Ajinkyatara sugar factory in Satara district. Near Murti, one tractor driver tried to overtake the tractor in front. The trolley overturned when the wheel of one tractor got caught in the other trolley.\nThe woman died on the spot. Other workers who were seriously injured have been admitted to a hospital in Baramati for treatment.","i":"illustration-3ffcf347a0","a":["Baramati","Baramati city","Baramati taluka"]},{"u":"pune/maharera-orders-siddharth-properties-pay-interest-delayed-possession.html","h":"MahaRERA orders Siddharth Properties to pay interest for delayed possession without OC","s":"MahaRERA ordered interest under Section 18 of RERA from January 1 to March 13, 2023, for the delayed possession of a Pune homebuyer’s flat in the Saarrthi Savvy Homes II project.","k":"MahaRERA order","c":"Business","t":"2026-11-13T16:00:19+05:30","g":["RERA","Siddharth Properties","Pune homebuyer","Saarrthi Savvy Homes II"],"b":"Siddharth Properties and its promoters must pay a Pune homebuyer interest for a flat in the Saarrthi Savvy Homes II project that was handed over late and without an Occupancy Certificate (OC), MahaRERA has directed.\nThe authority’s November 3, 2026 order held that a buyer who accepts possession does not lose the right to claim interest for the delay, especially when the flat is handed over without an OC. It ordered interest for the delay from January 1 to March 13, 2023, under Section 18 of RERA.\nThe buyer booked Flat No. 406 for approximately ₹49.27 lakh plus GST. The agreed possession deadline was December 31, 2022. Possession was actually handed over on March 13, 2023. The project had not received its OC.\nSeparate claims by the buyer for ₹5 lakh compensation and ₹75,000 legal expenses were rejected.","i":"illustration-274969e7ba","a":[]},{"u":"pune/camp-pmc-roadwork-allegedly-incomplete-outside-bishops-st-marys-schools.html","h":"PMC roadwork outside Bishop’s and St Mary’s schools in Camp allegedly incomplete for nearly two months","s":"PMC roadwork outside Bishop’s and St Mary’s schools in Camp is moving at a very slow pace, residents allege, despite earlier complaints and warnings.","k":"Camp","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-13T15:49:45+05:30","g":["PMC","Camp","Roadwork","Pune"],"b":"Students and residents are facing serious inconvenience outside Bishop’s and St Mary’s schools in Pune’s Camp area, where roadwork by the Pune Municipal Corporation’s (PMC) water supply department has allegedly been left incomplete for nearly two months.\nConstruction debris, potholes and excessive dust have made the stretch difficult to navigate, raising concerns over the safety of schoolchildren and pedestrians.\nResidents allege that, despite earlier complaints and warnings, the work is moving at a very slow pace. They have demanded that the road be restored immediately and have warned of protests if the civic administration does not act.","i":"","a":["Pune Camp","Camp","Pune Cantonment area"]},{"u":"pune/pune-maharera-orders-pinnacle-vastunirman-interest-32-sus-homebuyers.html","h":"MahaRERA orders Pinnacle Vastunirman to pay interest to 32 Sus homebuyers","s":"Pinnacle Vastunirman, a developer, has 60 days after obtaining the occupancy certificate to hand over possession, and must give each of 32 buyers ₹20,000 in litigation costs.","k":"Sus homebuyers","c":"Courts","t":"2026-11-13T15:38:45+05:30","g":["Maharashtra Real Estate Regulatory Authority","Pinnacle Vastunirman","Sus","Homebuyers","Pune"],"b":"Developer Pinnacle Vastunirman Pvt. Ltd. must pay interest for delayed possession to 32 homebuyers of Pinnacle Neelanchal Phase II in Sus, Pune, under an October 23, 2026 order of the Maharashtra Real Estate Regulatory Authority (MahaRERA).\nThe builder had cited financial difficulties, disputes with its financier and consent terms signed by certain buyers; MahaRERA rejected those arguments. It held that neither financial difficulties nor disputes with financiers can be used to avoid statutory obligations to homebuyers.\nAll 32 complainants are to be paid interest from their respective applicable dates until actual possession with an occupancy certificate. The developer must also give each buyer ₹20,000 in litigation costs, ₹6.4 lakh in all.\nMahaRERA rejected separate claims for rent reimbursement and compensation for mental agony. The builder has been given 60 days after obtaining the occupancy certificate to hand over possession.\nThe ruling reinforces homebuyers' rights under Section 18 of the Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Act.","i":"illustration-b5cb67bea1","a":["Sus","Sus Gaon"]},{"u":"pune/baner-pmc-stop-work-notices-regency-aavishkar-rohan-leher-1-access-road.html","h":"Baner: PMC issues stop-work notices to Regency Aavishkar, Rohan Leher-1 over missing access road","s":"Developers of the Regency Aavishkar and Rohan Leher-1 residential projects in Baner have been directed to immediately halt the construction work covered by notices issued under Section 267(1) of the Maharashtra Municipal Corporations Act by the Executive Engineer's office of the Pune Municipal Corporation's Building Development Department, Zone 3.","k":"Baner","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-13T15:28:03+05:30","g":["Baner","Pune Municipal Corporation","Stop-work notices","Regency Aavishkar","Rohan Leher-1"],"b":"The Pune Municipal Corporation (PMC) has issued stop-work notices, dated September 30, 2026, to the Regency Aavishkar and Rohan Leher-1 residential projects in Baner over a missing access road. The PMC has directed the developers to immediately halt the construction work covered by the notices.\nThe notices followed a complaint over the absence of a mandatory nine-metre-wide access road connecting certain properties to the main road. A complainant had approached the PMC seeking a proper access road for the affected properties.\nThe properties at the centre of the dispute are in Survey Numbers 54 and 55 in Baner. They have allegedly become landlocked because they have no independent and adequate access road to the main road.\nThe notices were issued by the Executive Engineer's office of the PMC's Building Development Department, Zone 3, under Section 267(1) of the Maharashtra Municipal Corporations Act and Section 54 of the Maharashtra Regional and Town Planning Act, 1966.\nThe PMC has warned that any violation of the orders could invite enforcement action with police assistance, with the expenses recovered from the developers concerned.","i":"illustration-6188d26f57","a":["Baner"]},{"u":"pune/pune-anti-extortion-squad-ii-arrest-man-allegedly-sexually-assaulting-boy.html","h":"Pune Police's Anti-Extortion Squad-II arrests man, 30, for allegedly sexually assaulting six-year-old boy","s":"A 30-year-old man accused of sexually assaulting a six-year-old boy in the city was apprehended near Pune Railway Station after an immediate search operation by the Crime Branch.","k":"Pune Police","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-13T15:17:31+05:30","g":["Pune Police","Anti-Extortion Squad-II","Bundgarden Police Station"],"b":"A 30-year-old man has been apprehended near Pune Railway Station and arrested by Pune Police's Anti-Extortion Squad-II for allegedly sexually assaulting a six-year-old boy in the city.\nThe boy's father lodged a complaint at Bundgarden Police Station. The matter came to light when, during a night-round operation, Police Inspector Yuvraj Hande, Lashkar Division's Night Round Officer, informed Assistant Police Inspector Shrikant Chavan over the phone.\nThe accused was traced after an immediate search operation by the Crime Branch. Squad personnel searched the Tadiwala Road and Pune Railway Station areas and took the man into custody.\nThe accused is being handed over to Bundgarden Police Station for further legal proceedings and investigation.","i":"illustration-f6a632991c","a":["Bund Garden"]},{"u":"pune/pune-family-allegedly-bursts-firecrackers-expressway-tunnel.html","h":"Family allegedly bursts firecrackers inside Mumbai-Pune Expressway tunnel","s":"Smoke in a tunnel can quickly reduce visibility, and a family was allegedly seen bursting firecrackers inside one on the Mumbai-Pune Expressway.","k":"Mumbai-Pune Expressway","c":"City","t":"2026-11-13T15:06:14+05:30","g":["Mumbai-Pune Expressway","Firecrackers","Road safety","Pune"],"b":"A family allegedly seen bursting firecrackers inside a tunnel on the Mumbai-Pune Expressway has raised questions about road safety and the enforcement of traffic rules.\nSmoke inside a tunnel, with limited ventilation, can quickly reduce visibility and put motorists at risk.\nAuthorities are being urged to identify those involved and take appropriate action if violations are established.","i":"","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pune-hot-water-suddenly-bubbles-up-valak-village-maval.html","h":"Hot water suddenly bubbles up from ground in Maval’s Valak village","s":"A large crowd of villagers gathered to see hot water bubbling from the ground in Valak village, Maval taluka, and its exact cause is not yet known.","k":"Valak village","c":"City","t":"2026-11-13T14:55:15+05:30","g":["Maval","Valak village","Hot water"],"b":"In Valak village of Maval taluka, Pune district, hot water suddenly bubbled up from the ground near a field. Around 7 am it is said to have been seen bubbling up near an agricultural field.\nThe unusual sight drew a large crowd of villagers, who gathered at the spot to see it.\nThe exact cause is not yet known. Further investigation is needed to find out whether it is a natural geothermal occurrence or something else.","i":"","a":["Maval","Mawal","Maval taluka"]},{"u":"pune/pune-airport-unauthorised-autorickshaws-back-fleecing-flyers-10-km.html","h":"Pune airport: unauthorised autorickshaws back, fleecing flyers; Rs1,200 for 10 km","s":"Aeromall's vice-president says unauthorised drivers have started using decoys: a person posing as a passenger persuades arriving flyers to hire an autorickshaw.","k":"Pune airport","c":"City","t":"2026-11-13T14:34:17+05:30","g":["Pune airport","Autorickshaws","Aeromall","Pune"],"b":"Unauthorised autorickshaws appear to be back at Pune airport, fleecing arriving flyers: in the early hours of November 5, a 40-year-old army veteran and businessman was offered a ride of barely 10 km for Rs1,200.\nThe ride was from outside the arrival area to Salunke Vihar Road. It was 2.30 am; he took a shuttle bus to Aeromall instead and hired a prepaid autorickshaw there for Rs435.\nAutorickshaw drivers had been barred from waiting outside the Pune airport terminal over complaints of passenger fleecing. Barely two months later, unauthorised operators appear to be approaching arriving passengers and demanding exorbitant fares. Airport authorities had barred autorickshaws from the terminal area in September after former MP Raju Shetti raised allegations of passenger exploitation.\nRegular flyers and authorised prepaid operators say the unauthorised drivers have gradually returned. A regular flyer said they now approach passengers walking towards Aeromall, some claiming to represent the prepaid service, mostly in the late evening.\nA prepaid operator said repeated complaints to airport authorities have changed nothing.\nWith CISF personnel closely monitoring the airport gates, the drivers have started using decoys, Aeromall's vice-president said: a driver drops off a person posing as a passenger, who then moves around persuading arriving flyers to hire an autorickshaw. The practice continues despite repeated efforts to keep unauthorised operators away, he said.","i":"illustration-7d28573c1a","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pune-court-sentences-haveli-man-life-imprisonment-killing-wife-axe.html","h":"Pune court sentences Haveli man to life imprisonment for killing wife with axe","s":"A Haveli taluka man received life imprisonment and a ₹10,000 fine from a Pune court over the axe killing of his wife.","k":"Haveli taluka","c":"Courts","t":"2026-11-13T14:23:28+05:30","g":["Pune court","Life imprisonment","Haveli","Lonikand Police Station"],"b":"A resident of Burkegaon in Haveli taluka has been sentenced by a Pune court to life imprisonment for killing his wife with an axe on July 23, 2024, over suspicion of her character.\nThe accused attacked his wife multiple times, causing fatal injuries, according to the prosecution.\nThe court relied on the daughter’s testimony, the accused’s extra-judicial confession and DNA evidence linking the victim’s blood to his shirt. Noting the brutality of the crime and the trauma suffered by the family, the court also imposed a fine of ₹10,000.\nThe case was registered at Lonikand Police Station.","i":"illustration-d66f813a7c","a":["Haveli","Haveli taluka","Haveli tehsil"]},{"u":"pune/ncp-mla-shankar-mandekar-rules-out-merger-talks.html","h":"‘I stand with Sunetra Pawar’: NCP MLA Shankar Mandekar rules out merger talks","s":"NCP MLA Shankar Mandekar said he would accept whatever Sunetra Pawar decides on the proposed merger.","k":"NCP merger","c":"Politics","t":"2026-11-13T14:12:54+05:30","g":["NCP","Shankar Mandekar","Sunetra Pawar","Pune"],"b":"No talks on the party’s merger took place at the meeting at Parth Pawar’s residence in Pune, which was limited to Diwali greetings and discussions about development work, NCP MLA Shankar Mandekar says.\nMandekar reaffirmed his support for Sunetra Pawar. He said he would accept whatever decision she takes on the proposed merger.","i":"","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pune-ncp-mlas-office-bearers-meet-parth-pawar-residence.html","h":"Pune NCP MLAs, office-bearers meet at Parth Pawar’s residence","s":"MLAs Datta Bharne, Shankar Mandekar, Mauli Katke and Chetan Tupe are attending an NCP meeting whose purpose and agenda have not yet been officially disclosed.","k":"Pune NCP","c":"Politics","t":"2026-11-13T13:57:11+05:30","g":["NCP","Parth Pawar","Pune MLAs"],"b":"Pune district NCP MLAs and senior party office-bearers have begun a meeting at Parth Pawar’s residence in Pune, with MLAs Datta Bharne, Shankar Mandekar, Mauli Katke and Chetan Tupe among those attending.\nOther senior party functionaries are attending too. The purpose and agenda of the meeting have not yet been officially disclosed.","i":"","a":[]},{"u":"pune/yerawada-deaf-mute-man-electrocuted-family-allegedly-drew-electricity-illegally.html","h":"Yerawada: deaf and mute man electrocuted; MSEDCL officials claim family allegedly drew electricity illegally","s":"Yerawada police have registered an accidental death case over a 29-year-old deaf and mute man's death by electrocution, and the exact cause of death is yet to be established.","k":"Yerawada electrocution","c":"Accidents and fires","t":"2026-11-13T13:44:41+05:30","g":["Yerawada","MSEDCL","Electrocution","Pune"],"b":"A 29-year-old deaf and mute man died of electrocution on the spot in his tin-sheet home in Yerawada's Jai Jawan Nagar, where he suffered a severe electric shock while walking towards the toilet.\nThe current is said to have reached an iron cupboard inside the house.\nMSEDCL officials claim the family had allegedly drawn electricity illegally from a feeder box, using a worn-out cable damaged at several places. MSEDCL Executive Engineer Deepak Patil said the damaged cable caused current to pass into the house. The family and residents have blamed MSEDCL negligence.\nAn electrical inspector visited the spot and conducted a panchnama. MSEDCL is awaiting the inspector's report to establish the exact circumstances.\nYerawada police have registered an accidental death case. The body was sent to Sassoon General Hospital for postmortem, and viscera has been preserved as the exact cause of death is yet to be established.\nSenior PI Yuvraj Nandre said police have sought a report from MSEDCL, which is still awaited.","i":"illustration-173bf679fb","a":["Yerawada","Yerwada","Yeravda","Yerawda","Yerwda"]},{"u":"pune/mumbai-pune-expressway-family-allegedly-bursts-firecrackers-tunnel.html","h":"Family allegedly bursts firecrackers in Mumbai–Pune Expressway tunnel","s":"Calls have been made for the authorities to identify those involved and register a case for endangering public safety, after a family was allegedly seen bursting firecrackers inside a tunnel.","k":"Mumbai–Pune Expressway","c":"City","t":"2026-11-13T13:33:25+05:30","g":["Mumbai–Pune Expressway","Firecrackers","Tunnel","Pune"],"b":"A family passing through a tunnel on the Mumbai–Pune Expressway was allegedly seen bursting firecrackers inside it.\nThe incident has raised serious concerns about the safety of commuters. Firecrackers set off inside a tunnel can create thick smoke and severely reduce visibility, putting the lives of other motorists at risk. Unlike in open spaces, the smoke cannot disperse immediately, which can create hazardous conditions for vehicles travelling behind.\nCalls have been made for the authorities to examine the footage, identify those involved and register a case against them for endangering public safety.","i":"","a":[]},{"u":"pune/alandi-youth-chased-hacked-murderous-koyta-attack-broad-daylight.html","h":"Alandi: youth chased, hacked in murderous koyta attack in broad daylight","s":"Two men carrying sharp weapons struck a youth repeatedly with a koyta in a populated area, and residents are in panic.","k":"Alandi","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-13T13:21:43+05:30","g":["Alandi","Koyta attack","Pune"],"b":"Two men chased a youth and hacked him in a murderous koyta attack in broad daylight within the Alandi Municipal Council limits at around 10:30 am on 13 November.\nThe two attackers were carrying sharp weapons and struck the youth repeatedly. The attack happened in a populated area in broad daylight, and panic has spread among residents.\nWhy the youth was attacked is not yet known. There is no official word yet on the injured youth's condition, the attackers' identity or any police action.","i":"","a":["Alandi","Alandi Devachi"]},{"u":"pune/tehseen-poonawalla-opposes-renaming-pune-phule-nagar.html","h":"‘Will not allow Pune to be renamed’: Tehseen Poonawalla opposes ‘Phule Nagar’","s":"The National OBC Mukti Morcha, which demanded the name ‘Phule Nagar’ for Pune ahead of Mahatma Phule’s 200th birth anniversary in 2027, has also sought a special one-day session of the state legislature.","k":"Phule Nagar","c":"Politics","t":"2026-11-13T13:10:44+05:30","g":["Phule Nagar","Tehseen Poonawalla","Mahatma Phule","National OBC Mukti Morcha"],"b":"Tehseen Poonawalla has strongly opposed the National OBC Mukti Morcha’s demand that Pune be renamed ‘Phule Nagar’, saying the city should not be renamed and that its historical identity must be preserved.\nThe demand is in honour of social reformer Mahatma Jyotirao Phule. Taking to social media, Poonawalla said, “We will NOT allow our Pune to be renamed after Jyotirao Phule ji.”\nPoonawalla argued that Pune derives its name from the over 1,000-year-old Punyeshwar Mahadev Temple, which stood on the banks of the Mutha River. He argued too that renaming the city would erase an identity tied to its history, investments, opportunities and cultural heritage.\nPoonawalla said in his post, “We have immense respect for Jyotirao Phule ji, but we will NOT allow any renaming!”\nPoonawalla’s reaction comes after the Morcha demanded that Pune be renamed ‘Phule Nagar’ ahead of Mahatma Phule’s 200th birth anniversary in 2027.\nA delegation of the organisation recently met Chief Minister Devendra Fadnavis in Nagpur and submitted a memorandum seeking a state government resolution supporting the name change. The organisation has also sought a posthumous Bharat Ratna for Mahatma Phule and a special one-day session of the state legislature to discuss his contributions.","i":"","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pune-879-swine-flu-h1n1-cases-highest-in-maharashtra.html","h":"Pune reports 879 swine flu (H1N1) cases, highest in Maharashtra","s":"Nagpur has reported the highest H1N1-related toll in Maharashtra, 12, with 35 deaths recorded across the state.","k":"Swine flu","c":"City","t":"2026-11-13T13:00:09+05:30","g":["Swine flu","H1N1","Pune","Maharashtra"],"b":"Pune has reported 879 swine flu (H1N1) cases, the most in Maharashtra; Mumbai has recorded 648 and Nagpur 493.\nMaharashtra has recorded 35 H1N1-related deaths. Nagpur has reported the highest toll at 12, followed by Nashik (8), Pune (3) and Navi Mumbai (1).\nH1N1 is an influenza virus originally associated with pigs. It spreads mainly from person to person through respiratory droplets and aerosols when an infected person coughs, sneezes or talks. Contact with pigs or eating properly cooked pork does not usually cause human infections.\nTo stay safe: wear a mask in crowded places, wash your hands frequently, cover your mouth and nose while coughing or sneezing, avoid close contact with infected people and stay home if you have flu symptoms. Get vaccinated as advised by a healthcare professional, avoid self-medication and consult a doctor, especially if symptoms are severe or you are at higher risk.\nThe figures are from health department data.","i":"illustration-cda943d41c","a":[]},{"u":"pune/seven-sinhgad-society-colleges-taken-over-by-state-three-years.html","h":"Seven Sinhgad society colleges taken over by state government for three years, citing non-payment of salaries","s":"The divisional joint director of higher education, Pune, is now administrator of seven permanently unaided colleges run by the Pune-based Sinhgad Technical Education Society, whose 44 institutions the Bombay High Court has ordered investigated.","k":"Sinhgad colleges","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-13T12:48:03+05:30","g":["Sinhgad Technical Education Society","Sinhgad colleges","Bombay High Court","Higher education","Pune"],"b":"The state government has taken over management of seven colleges run by the Pune-based Sinhgad Technical Education Society for three years, through a notification the Directorate of Higher Education issued on Thursday under the Maharashtra Educational Institutions (Management) Act, 1976.\nThe government is citing prolonged non-payment of salaries and retirement benefits to employees and the impact on students’ education. The divisional joint director of higher education, Pune, has been appointed administrator of the seven permanently unaided colleges.\nHigher education director Shailendra Deolankar said the management had failed to discharge its responsibilities and that its functioning was affecting students’ academic interests.\nDespite court directions in July 2025 and August 2026 and repeated reminders, the management did not clear employees’ dues, the notification states. It also notes that at least 13 employees died by suicide amid financial distress linked to prolonged non-payment of salaries. The society did not respond to a show-cause notice issued on November 5.\nThe Bombay High Court on Tuesday directed the CBI, the Enforcement Directorate and Income Tax authorities to investigate the affairs of 44 institutions run by the society, and restrained its trustees from dealing with any of their properties pending the probe.\nThe seven colleges are Sinhgad College of Law (Ambegaon), Shrimati Kashibai Navale College of Education (Kusgaon, Lonavla), Sinhgad College of Arts and Commerce (Narhe), Nirvrutti Babaji Navale College of Commerce and Science (Kusgaon), Sinhgad College of Commerce (Kondhwa), Shrimati Kashibai Navale College of Commerce (Erandwane) and Sinhgad College of Science (Ambegaon Budruk).","i":"illustration-7e5fdaa21f","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pmpml-older-buses-cctv-cameras-said-to-be-faulty-or-missing-inquiry.html","h":"CCTV cameras in several older PMPML buses said to be faulty or missing; inquiry promised","s":"PMPML buses carry nearly 13 lakh passengers every day; commuters are demanding accountability, and PMPML officials say cameras have been installed in newer buses.","k":"PMPML buses","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-13T12:35:57+05:30","g":["PMPML","CCTV","Passenger safety","Pune buses"],"b":"Cameras in several older buses of Pune Mahanagar Parivahan Mahamandal Limited (PMPML) are said to be faulty, switched off or missing, and commuters have raised concerns over the lack of functional cameras and proper monitoring.\nPassenger safety on PMPML buses has come under scrutiny. Nearly 13 lakh passengers travel on PMPML buses every day.\nCCTV surveillance was introduced to prevent theft, harassment and pickpocketing. Commuters are demanding accountability and asking authorities to ensure that cameras are installed, maintained and regularly monitored across the fleet.\nPMPML officials have stated that cameras have been installed in newer buses, and that an inquiry will be conducted into the issues raised.","i":"illustration-f18a21ecd8","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pune-karvenagar-woman-75-allegedly-cheated-32-lakh-digital-arrest-fraud.html","h":"Karvenagar woman, 75, allegedly cheated of ₹32 lakh in digital arrest fraud","s":"Fearing arrest, a 75-year-old Karvenagar woman allegedly made RTGS transfers totalling ₹32 lakh to bank accounts provided by cyber fraudsters.","k":"Karvenagar","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-13T12:25:24+05:30","g":["Karvenagar","Digital arrest","Cyber fraud","Warje police"],"b":"Warje police registered a case on November 11 against unidentified cyber fraudsters who allegedly cheated a 75-year-old Karvenagar woman of ₹32 lakh and threatened her with digital arrest.\nPolice say unidentified persons phoned her on October 6. The callers allegedly told her that her Aadhaar card details had been misused to facilitate a ₹2-crore financial fraud at a Canara Bank branch in Nashik. They also allegedly claimed the money had been transferred to her bank account.\nThey warned her that a warrant would be issued against her and that she would be arrested if she failed to cooperate. They also warned her that her properties and bank accounts would be frozen.\nFearing arrest, she allegedly transferred money through RTGS to bank accounts provided by the fraudsters on multiple occasions, a total of ₹32 lakh between October 6 and November 6. The fraudsters allegedly kept demanding more even after receiving the money.\nSuspicious of the repeated demands, she made inquiries, realised she had been duped and lodged a complaint. Police inspector Suvarna Hulwan is investigating the case.","i":"illustration-1829d02683","a":["Karvenagar"]},{"u":"pune/viman-nagar-22-year-old-dies-after-allegedly-assaulted-over-firecrackers.html","h":"Viman Nagar: 22-year-old dies after being allegedly brutally assaulted over firecrackers","s":"Airport Police have added murder charges to a case in which a 22-year-old man died after being allegedly assaulted; four accused aged between 18 and 20 have been arrested.","k":"Viman Nagar","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-13T11:49:29+05:30","g":["Viman Nagar","Airport Police","Murder charges","Firecrackers"],"b":"A group of youths allegedly brutally assaulted a 22-year-old man over bursting firecrackers outside Rose Garden Society on Kayra Road in Viman Nagar at around 9.30 pm on November 8.\nHe died while undergoing treatment at Sassoon General Hospital on Thursday afternoon. The young man was a resident of Kalwad Vasti on Lohgaon Road.\nPolice say the man was bursting firecrackers with his friends when another group of four youths was doing the same a short distance away. When some firecrackers landed near them, he asked the group to burst them further away, police say. An argument followed; when he objected to the abusive language used by the group, the accused allegedly attacked him with kicks and punches.\nThe group then allegedly picked up a wooden bamboo lying by the roadside and repeatedly struck him on his head, back, hands and face and fled.\nHis friends rushed him to a private hospital and later shifted him to Sassoon General Hospital. Doctors performed surgery, but his condition did not improve.\nAirport Police have added murder charges to the case, initially registered as an attempt to murder case against 11 persons. Four accused aged between 18 and 20 have been arrested, and a minor has been detained. Six other accused have been booked, and efforts are underway to trace them.\n“There is darkness at the spot where the incident occurred, and there are no CCTV cameras in the vicinity,” said investigating officer Police Sub-Inspector Nitin Rathod.","i":"illustration-e1b4ea34bf","a":["Viman Nagar","Vimantal"]},{"u":"pune/maharashtra-dairies-consider-milk-price-hike-from-nov-15.html","h":"Maharashtra dairies consider milk price hike from Nov 15; meeting to decide amount","s":"A possible milk price hike in Maharashtra follows recent increases by Amul and Mother Dairy, and its size is yet to be finalised.","k":"Milk prices","c":"Business","t":"2026-11-13T11:37:21+05:30","g":["Milk price","Dairy","Maharashtra","Katraj Dairy"],"b":"Pouch milk (cow and buffalo) may soon cost more in Maharashtra, with several private and cooperative dairies considering a price hike from Nov 15 and the amount to be decided at a meeting of dairy operators on Friday.\nThe size of the increase is yet to be finalised. The meeting will be held at the training centre of the Pune District Cooperative Milk Producers' Union (Katraj Dairy) on Pune-Satara Road, and private and cooperative players, including local brands such as Chitale and Katraj, are expected to take part.\nPrakash Kutwal, secretary of the Maharashtra Rajya Dudh Vyavsayik Sanghatana, which convened the meeting, said the procurement rate paid to farmers was earlier raised by Rs 5 but the consumer price rose by only Rs 2. He said packaging, diesel, gas and other raw materials have since become costlier.\nKutwal said the revision should not be attributed solely to the drought. He cautioned against speculating on the amount before Friday's meeting.\nThe move follows recent hikes by Amul and Mother Dairy. Amul raised Amul Taaza toned milk by Rs 2 a litre and Amul Gold by Rs 4 a litre from Nov 12, and Mother Dairy raised its milk prices in the Mumbai region by Rs 2 to Rs 6 a litre.","i":"illustration-a55cd71678","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pune-pickup-catches-fire-pulachi-wadi-after-firecracker-said-to-have-landed.html","h":"Pickup catches fire near Z Bridge in Pulachi Wadi after firecracker is said to have landed on it","s":"A fire damaged the front portion and roof of a Mahindra Zeno pickup on the riverside road beneath Z Bridge.","k":"Pulachi Wadi","c":"Accidents and fires","t":"2026-11-13T11:16:06+05:30","g":["Pune fire","Z Bridge","Pulachi Wadi"],"b":"A Mahindra Zeno pickup caught fire in Pune around 2 AM after a firecracker is said to have landed on it.\nThe vehicle was on the riverside road near Bhide Bridge, beneath Z Bridge, in the Pulachi Wadi area.\nThe fire damaged its front portion and roof, causing significant losses.","i":"","a":[]},{"u":"pune/supriya-sule-ruled-out-ncp-merger-draw-curtains-after-ajit-pawar-death.html","h":"Supriya Sule ruled out NCP merger, decided to “draw the curtains” after Ajit Pawar’s death","s":"NCP (SP) working president Supriya Sule said in Pune that she decided to draw “the curtains” on the NCP merger after Ajit Pawar’s death.","k":"NCP merger","c":"Politics","t":"2026-11-13T11:05:07+05:30","g":["Supriya Sule","NCP","Ajit Pawar","Sharad Pawar"],"b":"Supriya Sule, working president of NCP (SP), ruled out on Thursday any merger of the Sharad Pawar-led NCP with the rival party led by the late Ajit Pawar, who died in a plane crash on January 28. She said she had received no fresh merger proposal.\n“Discussions on the merger were on when Ajit Pawar was alive, and the entire world knew about them,” Sule said in Pune. “The day my cousin died, and following the developments that unfolded a few days after his death, I decided to draw the curtains on the issue of merger. It ended with my cousin’s death.”\nOn Wednesday, NCP president Sunetra Pawar declined to clarify whether a merger was possible, saying matters would become clear at the appropriate time.\nState NCP president Sunil Tatkare has claimed the merger would have taken place had Ajit Pawar been alive.\nTatkare and state minister Hasan Mushrif said on Thursday they would soon meet Sharad Pawar in Mumbai.\n“I will meet Pawar Saheb to enquire about his health when I visit Mumbai,” Tatkare said. Mushrif said, “We will abide by the decision Sunetra Pawar takes on the merger.”","i":"","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pune-six-leopard-attacks-junnar-bikers-two-weeks-harvest-encounters.html","h":"Six leopard attacks on Junnar bikers in two weeks as harvest drives up encounters","s":"None of the six leopard attacks on motorcycle riders in the Junnar forest division in two weeks was fatal, said assistant conservator of forests Smita Rajhans.","k":"Junnar","c":"City","t":"2026-11-13T10:54:32+05:30","g":["Junnar","Leopard attacks","Otur","Shirur","Sugarcane"],"b":"Leopards attacked bikers on motorcycles six times in two weeks in the Junnar forest division, with the incidents recorded mainly in the Otur and Shirur forest ranges, as sugarcane harvesting gathers pace.\nForest officials said the incidents have largely occurred during evening hours, when leopards move between sugarcane fields and adjoining habitats. As standing sugarcane is cleared during the crushing season, the animals are more likely to move across village roads.\nSmita Rajhans, assistant conservator of forests, said none of the six incidents resulted in a fatality.\n“These attacks happen when motorcycles suddenly appear while leopards are moving or crossing roads. The animals get startled and react defensively. In none of these incidents did the leopard chase the motorcycle,” she said.\nIn areas where leopard movement is frequently reported, farmers and villagers have been advised to avoid travelling during night hours.\nNaresh Dhome, former sarpanch of Pimparkhed village, called for identifying vulnerable road stretches near sugarcane plantations, installing warning boards and coordinating harvesting with forest officials. Two fatal attacks were reported last year in Pimparkhed village.\nThe forest department has urged villagers to report leopard sightings to it rather than approach or provoke the animals, and to take care on vulnerable stretches.","i":"illustration-e35a76837c","a":["Junnar","Junnar taluka","Otur","Shirur","Shirur taluka","Shirur town","Ghodnadi"]},{"u":"pune/pune-air-worse-than-delhi-bhosari-index-427.html","h":"Pune’s air worse than Delhi’s, with Bhosari’s index at 427","s":"Shivajinagar followed Bhosari’s 427 with 250 and Nigdi with 214 on the air quality index, in readings from the portal of the Indian Institute of Tropical Meteorology.","k":"Air quality","c":"City","t":"2026-11-13T10:43:57+05:30","g":["Pune","Bhosari","Air quality","Diwali pollution"],"b":"On Thursday, Bhosari’s air quality index stood at 427 while Delhi’s was 320, so Pune’s air was worse than Delhi’s.\nShivajinagar followed at 250 and Nigdi at 214. In parts of the city, air quality has slipped into the highly polluted category.\nDiwali’s pollution still hangs in the air, and vehicle pollution is now adding to it. This Diwali, the highest firecracker pollution was measured in Pune city, and it has risen further since the festival ended, as more traffic on the roads means more pollution from burning fuel.\nThe levels of PM10 and PM2.5 particulate matter and of carbon monoxide in the city’s air have risen sharply.\nThe readings are from the air quality index portal of the Indian Institute of Tropical Meteorology (IITM), which measures air quality in Delhi, Mumbai, Pune, Ahmedabad and Kolkata.","i":"illustration-315742d7c5","a":["Bhosari"]},{"u":"pune/two-daily-wage-workers-killed-motorcycle-hits-parked-truck-chandni-chowk.html","h":"Two daily wage workers killed as motorcycle hits parked truck near Chandni Chowk, Pune","s":"Two daily wage workers died when their motorcycle hit a parked container truck, and a case of causing death by negligence has been registered against a truck driver.","k":"Chandni Chowk","c":"Accidents and fires","t":"2026-11-13T10:32:40+05:30","g":["Chandni Chowk","Pune","Bavdhan police","Katraj-Dehu Road bypass"],"b":"Two daily wage workers, aged 26 and 20, were killed in the early hours of Monday when their motorcycle hit a parked container truck on the Katraj-Dehu Road bypass near Chandni Chowk in Pune. Police sub-inspector Sarang Thakare of Bavdhan police gave the details.\nThe two lived in Kalewadi and hailed from Beed district. On Sunday night they had set out on the motorcycle for Chikkodi in Karnataka to meet the rider's parents. The rider failed to notice the stationary container truck and rammed into it; both were killed on the spot.\nPolice found that the truck driver had parked the vehicle without switching on its indicators. After the accident, he fled the scene instead of helping the victims. A case of causing death by negligence has been registered against the driver.","i":"illustration-638b3bfcfb","a":["Bavdhan","Bawdhan","Bavdhan Budruk"]},{"u":"pune/bombay-hc-orders-cbi-ed-income-tax-probe-sinhgad-trust-freezes-accounts.html","h":"Bombay HC orders CBI, ED, Income Tax probe into Sinhgad trust, freezes accounts","s":"Bank accounts and investments of the Sinhgad trust and its trustees stand frozen, and the state education department is to take over its institutions or shift their students.","k":"Sinhgad trust","c":"Courts","t":"2026-11-12T23:09:09+05:30","g":["Sinhgad Technical Education Society","Bombay High Court","Maruti Navale","Pune"],"b":"The Bombay High Court ordered the CBI, ED and Income Tax department on 10 November to investigate Sinhgad Technical Education Society, its 44 institutions and its trustees over suspected financial irregularities and possible fund diversion.\nA special bench of Justices G S Kulkarni and Advait M Sethna was hearing about 220 petitions and contempt cases filed by the society's employees.\nThe order followed managing trustee Maruti Navale's failure to pay ₹60.65 crore by 7 November towards employees' dues, as he had undertaken to the court. The court called this an abuse of the legal process.\nThe court noted the dues owed to employees were stated to exceed ₹400 crore. It froze the bank accounts and investments of the trust and its trustees, ordered the trustees to surrender their passports and barred them from leaving Pune.\nThe state education department is to take over the institutions or shift their students.\nNavale said the trust accepts the verdict and will cooperate with the agencies. He said he has instructed the heads of all 44 institutions to extend full cooperation.\n“We accept the verdict of the hon’ble high court and shall cooperate with the agencies in their endeavours.”\nMaruti Navale said\nThe matter is next heard on 19 November.","i":"","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pune-car-overturns-in-pimple-saudagar-after-driver-loses-control.html","h":"Car overturns in Pimple Saudagar after driver loses control, vehicle severely damaged","s":"A car overturned and was severely damaged in Pimple Saudagar after its driver lost control.","k":"Pimple Saudagar","c":"Accidents and fires","t":"2026-11-12T22:57:46+05:30","g":["Pimple Saudagar","Pimpri-Chinchwad","car overturned"],"b":"In Pimple Saudagar, Pimpri-Chinchwad, a car overturned after its driver lost control of it.\nThe car was severely damaged.","i":"","a":["Pimple Saudagar"]},{"u":"pune/kolwadi-autorickshaw-driver-allegedly-beaten-to-death-father-in-law.html","h":"Kolwadi family dispute: autorickshaw driver allegedly beaten to death by father-in-law, grandfather-in-law","s":"Police have registered a murder case against the 45-year-old father-in-law and 65-year-old grandfather-in-law of an autorickshaw driver whose relatives had told doctors he was hurt in a motorcycle fall.","k":"Kolwadi","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-12T22:46:01+05:30","g":["Pune","Kolwadi","Lonikand","Autorickshaw driver","Murder case"],"b":"A 24-year-old autorickshaw driver’s death near Pune, first described as a motorcycle accident, is now a murder case: police say he was allegedly beaten to death by his father-in-law and grandfather-in-law following a family dispute in Kolwadi village on the outskirts of Pune.\nAccording to the FIR, registered on November 10, the driver and his wife had an argument on the evening of November 9, after which she left their home. Around 8.30 pm, the father-in-law and grandfather-in-law allegedly brought him, unconscious and injured, in an autorickshaw to the area below his brother’s residence and said he had suddenly fallen.\nHis brother, the complainant, alleged that the two, angry over the couple’s dispute, assaulted him on his head, hands and back with a weapon.\nHe was taken to a private hospital in Kharadi with multiple injuries, where he was declared dead. His relatives had told doctors that he was hurt in a fall from a motorcycle in the Pawarvasti area.\nSenior Inspector Sunita Rokade, in charge of Lonikand police station, said that when police visited the spot identified by the two men there were no signs of an accident and no witnesses. Rokade said the postmortem showed the head injury could not have been caused by a motorcycle fall.\nPolice have registered a murder case against the father-in-law, 45, and the grandfather-in-law, 65, under Sections 103(1) and 3(5) of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita.","i":"illustration-de42919eff","a":["Lonikand"]},{"u":"pune/pune-cng-99-a-kg-from-midnight-household-png-prices-raised.html","h":"Pune: CNG at ₹99 a kg from midnight, household PNG prices raised too","s":"Pune's CNG price has risen five times in a year and household PNG's twice, a total rise of ₹8.25 for CNG against ₹2.35 for PNG.","k":"CNG and PNG prices","c":"Business","t":"2026-11-12T22:33:53+05:30","g":["Pune","CNG","PNG","MNGL"],"b":"MNGL India Limited has raised CNG prices by ₹1.25 a kg and household PNG prices by ₹1.50, taking CNG to ₹99 a kg in Pune and Pimpri-Chinchwad from midnight.\nThe new rates apply from midnight. CNG is ₹99.00 a kg in Pune, Pimpri-Chinchwad, Chakan, Talegaon and Hinjewadi. Household piped gas (PNG) in the Pune and Pimpri-Chinchwad municipal corporation areas will cost ₹53.00 per SCM.\nCNG prices in Pune have gone up five times in the past year, and household PNG prices twice. CNG was ₹90.75 a kg in October 2025 and has risen in stages since May 2026 to ₹99. That is a total rise of ₹8.25 in the year, against ₹2.35 for PNG.\nMNGL said it had to raise prices because imported natural gas (RLNG) now makes up a larger share of its total gas supply, which has raised its gas purchase and import costs.","i":"illustration-2b5d102030","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pune-clean-city-ranking-takes-a-hit-10th-to-27th-swachh-survekshan.html","h":"Pune’s clean city ranking takes a hit: from 10th to 27th in Swachh Survekshan","s":"Pune ranks 18th of 50 cities in the Swachh Vayu Survekshan, a rating of efforts to improve air quality.","k":"Swachh Survekshan","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-12T22:23:15+05:30","g":["Pune","Swachh Survekshan","Swachh Vayu Survekshan","PMC"],"b":"In the Centre’s Swachh Survekshan, Pune has slipped from 10th to 27th position among cities with a population of over one lakh. In the category of cities with more than 10 lakh population, Pune has dropped from eighth last year to 12th this year. It is out of the top 10 in both categories.\nIn the Swachh Vayu Survekshan, which assesses efforts to improve air quality, Pune has secured 18th position among 50 cities. This has brought renewed attention to the ₹281 crore the Central Government allocated to control air pollution in Pune.\nThe Pune Municipal Corporation (PMC) has issued tenders worth hundreds of crores of rupees for sanitation, waste management and processing infrastructure over the past several years, yet garbage-related problems persist.\nThe PMC continues to struggle to meet stricter criteria that now include 100% treatment of the sewage generated in the city and keeping water bodies free from pollution.\nConcerns have also been raised that cleanliness efforts are often intensified only during the survey period, and that municipal employees are allegedly being directed to register participation in the citizen feedback process.","i":"illustration-cf1d6fa747","a":[]},{"u":"pune/acb-books-ghotawade-circle-officer-alleged-bribe-demand-land-record-entries.html","h":"ACB books Ghotawade circle officer in Mulshi over alleged bribe demand for land record entries","s":"A 40-year-old man who bought two parcels of land in Mulshi taluka alleged that Ghotawade circle officer Rohini Shashank Gupte demanded ₹20,000 in total for the two 7/12 and mutation entries.","k":"Mulshi taluka","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-12T22:07:24+05:30","g":["Anti-Corruption Bureau","Mulshi","Ghotawade","Land records"],"b":"A case against Rohini Shashank Gupte, 57, the circle officer at Ghotawade in Mulshi taluka, for allegedly demanding a bribe in connection with entries in land records, was registered on November 12 by the Pune unit of the Anti-Corruption Bureau (ACB) at Paud police station under Pune Rural Police.\nIt was registered under Section 7 of the Prevention of Corruption Act, as crime register number 342/2026. The information is from the ACB’s press note.\nThe complainant, a 40-year-old man, had bought two parcels of land in Mulshi taluka. He alleged that Gupte called him on his mobile phone and demanded ₹5,000 each for herself and the talathi for each of the two 7/12 and mutation entries, ₹20,000 in total. He approached the ACB on July 24, 2026.\nThe ACB says that during a verification on July 28, 2026, Gupte allegedly demanded ₹5,000 for herself in the presence of witnesses and agreed to accept it. She has been taken into custody, and since it was after sunset, the process of obtaining the court’s permission for her arrest was underway.\nThe ACB has appealed to citizens to report bribe demands by public servants on the 1064 helpline, the Pune ACB office on 020-26132802, or WhatsApp 9403781064.","i":"illustration-8dde7c284c","a":["Mulshi","Mulshi taluka","Ghotawade"]},{"u":"pune/rohit-pawar-slams-cm-fadnavis-merger-remarks-alleges-bjp-blackmail.html","h":"‘Arrogance of power’: Rohit Pawar slams CM Fadnavis over NCP merger remarks, alleges BJP ‘blackmail’","s":"NCP (SP) MLA Rohit Pawar claimed in a post on X that the late NCP leader Ajit Pawar did not give in to the BJP even slightly despite attempts to “blackmail” him.","k":"NCP merger","c":"Politics","t":"2026-11-12T21:26:48+05:30","g":["Rohit Pawar","Devendra Fadnavis","NCP","Mundhwa"],"b":"Rohit Pawar, an NCP (SP) MLA, slammed Chief Minister Devendra Fadnavis over his NCP merger remarks and, on Thursday, alleged that they reflected the “arrogance” of those in power.\nOn Tuesday, Fadnavis said that only Sharad Pawar and Deputy Chief Minister Sunetra Pawar, who head the rival factions, could clarify whether their parties would reunite. A merger, he also said, cannot happen without consulting the BJP, which heads the ruling coalition.\nIn a post on X, Rohit Pawar referred to the Mundhwa case and the Pimpri Chinchwad Municipal Corporation (PCMC) elections. He claimed that despite attempts to “blackmail” Ajit Pawar over the issue, the late NCP leader had not given in to the BJP even slightly.\n“Who was blackmailing Ajitdada, and who gave orders to blackmail him?”\nRohit Pawar asked\nHe said the BJP and its leaders, whose politics he claimed were built on “blackmail”, should refrain from commenting on bringing the two NCP factions together.\nParth Pawar, Ajit Pawar’s son and a Rajya Sabha MP, is a majority partner in Amadea Enterprises LLP. The firm bought a 40-acre government-owned land parcel in Pune’s Mundhwa area for Rs 300 crore, much lower than its actual value, and was also allegedly exempted from paying Rs 21 crore in stamp duty. An FIR has been registered against several persons for allegedly facilitating the transaction.\nLeaders of the Sunetra Pawar-led NCP, including Praful Patel and Parth Pawar, met Sharad Pawar last week. There has been speculation about a merger of the two factions since Ajit Pawar died in a plane crash in January.","i":"","a":["Mundhwa","Mundhawa"]},{"u":"pune/cockroach-spotted-good-luck-cafe-pune-airport-outlet.html","h":"Cockroach spotted at Good Luck Cafe’s Pune Airport outlet","s":"Questions on sanitation standards at Good Luck Cafe’s outlets, including its main branch, follow a cockroach sighting at its Pune Airport outlet.","k":"Pune Airport","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-12T20:40:59+05:30","g":["Good Luck Cafe","Pune Airport","Food hygiene","Cockroach"],"b":"Serious concerns over food hygiene and cleanliness have followed a cockroach spotted at Good Luck Cafe’s Pune Airport outlet.\nSanitation standards across Good Luck Cafe’s outlets, the main branch included, are now being questioned.","i":"","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pune-grand-tour-pmc-sets-november-20-road-excavation-deadline.html","h":"PMC sets November 20 deadline for road excavation on Pune Grand Tour routes, warns of fourfold charges","s":"Contractors who miss set milestones on the Pune Grand Tour road works will be issued show-cause notices, and their contracts could be cancelled if there is no substantial improvement by the next review meeting.","k":"Pune Grand Tour","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-12T20:14:57+05:30","g":["Pune Grand Tour","PMC","Road excavation","Utility agencies"],"b":"All utility agencies have until November 20 to complete road excavation on the city’s designated cycling routes for the Pune Grand Tour international cycling event, the Pune Municipal Corporation (PMC) has told them. At the joint review meeting on Thursday, Municipal Commissioner Naval Kishore Ram warned that any excavation after the deadline will attract fourfold charges: at least four times the prevailing rates, with no fresh permissions granted.\nRam and Pune District Collector Jitendra Dudi held the meeting to review road, resurfacing, footpath, cycle track and beautification works being carried out in four packages for the event.\nThe civic administration expressed strong displeasure that utility agencies including Maharashtra Natural Gas Limited (MNGL), Maharashtra State Electricity Distribution Company Limited (MSEDCL), Dinesh Engineering and Allied Digital have not completed excavation within the set timelines despite having permissions. These agencies have been asked to give written undertakings on the work they will finish, the manpower they will deploy and the number of teams they will mobilise.\nShow-cause notices will be issued to contractors who miss the set milestones. If progress remains unsatisfactory, penalties will follow under tender conditions, and contracts could be cancelled if there is no substantial improvement by the next review meeting. Completing only the asphalt layer will not count as completing a road stretch.\nWard officers, zonal deputy commissioners and the anti-encroachment department have been directed to remove encroachments, hawkers and other obstructions along the entire cycling route.","i":"","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pune-district-received-1-63-988-sir-applications-deadline-13-november.html","h":"Pune district received 1,63,988 SIR applications; deadline is 13 November","s":"Form 6, used to add names to the electoral roll, accounts for nearly 69% of the applications Pune district had received under the Special Intensive Revision of electoral rolls.","k":"Electoral rolls","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-12T20:04:17+05:30","g":["SIR","Electoral rolls","Pune district","Form 6"],"b":"Figures from the Pune District Election Office show that Pune district had received 1,63,988 applications across three forms as of 12 November. The SIR deadline is 13 November, with one day left to file claims and objections.\nForm 6, used to add names to the electoral roll, drew the most applications, 1,12,299, nearly 69% of the total. Form 7, used to object to names and seek deletions, drew 8,781, and Form 8, for corrections to existing entries, drew 42,908.\nPune District Deputy Collector and Deputy Election Officer Meenal Kalaskar appealed to voters: “I appeal to every voter to check their name and complete the enrolment process by November 13. Do not panic if you are temporarily staying abroad or away from your registered address. Even after the final roll is published on November 30, the SSR process will allow continuous updating.”\nThe notice phase and disposal of claims and objections will run until 25 November. The final electoral roll is scheduled for publication on 30 November.","i":"illustration-caac602027","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pune-two-wheeler-rider-dies-speeding-vehicle-katraj-warje-bypass-bridge.html","h":"Two-wheeler rider dies after speeding vehicle hits him on Katraj–Warje bypass bridge; driver flees","s":"Warje Malwadi police are investigating a case against an unidentified driver who fled after a speeding vehicle hit a two-wheeler rider on the Katraj–Warje bypass bridge.","k":"Katraj–Warje bypass","c":"Accidents and fires","t":"2026-11-12T19:38:41+05:30","g":["Pune","Katraj–Warje bypass bridge","Warje Malwadi police","Two-wheeler rider"],"b":"A 51-year-old two-wheeler rider from Dattanagar, Ambegaon Budruk, died after a speeding unidentified vehicle hit him on the Katraj–Warje bypass bridge at around 3:30 pm on 10 November.\nThe vehicle hit his two-wheeler hard, and he was seriously injured in the crash. The driver did not stop after the accident and fled the scene without helping the injured man.\nHis nephew filed a complaint at Warje Malwadi police station, and a case has been registered against the unidentified driver. Warje Malwadi police are investigating further.","i":"illustration-9168ae61c2","a":["Katraj","Warje","Warje Malwadi"]},{"u":"pune/pune-locals-say-thousands-litres-water-going-to-waste-chandni-chowk.html","h":"Locals say thousands of litres of water going to waste at Chandni Chowk","s":"Residents dispute what PMC officials are said to have stated, that water flowing from a hillside near a newly constructed water tank could be residential drainage.","k":"Chandni Chowk","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-12T19:27:56+05:30","g":["Chandni Chowk","NDA Chowk","PMC","Water seepage"],"b":"Locals say thousands of litres of water are going to waste near NDA Chowk at Chandni Chowk in Pune, where residents have raised concerns over continuous seepage from a hillside near a newly constructed water tank.\nLocals claim the leakage began after the new tank was built. Locals claim it continues even two months after the monsoon ended, with the water flowing into nearby drains instead of being conserved or reused.\nPMC officials are said to have stated that the area falls within a Biodiversity Park zone and that the flowing water could be residential drainage. Residents dispute this, arguing that the continuous flow does not appear to be ordinary drainage discharge.\nHemant Jagtap, an engineer from the water supply department, said the water seeping through the rocks since the road-widening work had been tested and found unfit for drinking.\nResidents have suggested that the water be pumped uphill and reused for watering trees planted on the hill near the Bavdhan water tank. Locals are demanding a solution before Metro construction work begins in the area, and an online complaint has been submitted to the civic body.","i":"","a":[]},{"u":"pune/shirur-farmer-alleges-police-sub-inspector-assaulted-him-outpost.html","h":"Shirur (Pune district) farmer alleges police sub-inspector assaulted him at outpost; inquiry under way","s":"Senior police officers are inquiring into a complaint by a Takali Haji farmer, who alleges a police sub-inspector slapped him, abused him and threatened to kill him.","k":"Shirur","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-12T19:01:58+05:30","g":["Shirur","Takali Haji","Police sub-inspector","Farmer"],"b":"A farmer from Takali Haji in Shirur taluka, Pune district, alleges in a written complaint to the Sub-Divisional Police Officer that Police Sub-Inspector Govind Khating assaulted him at the Takali Haji outpost.\nHe alleges that Khating slapped him, abused him, snatched his mobile phone and threatened to kill him. He says in the complaint that he hears less in his left ear since the beating and that his jaw is swollen.\nAccording to his complaint, a farmland dispute with his cousin's family on 31 October led to complaints from both sides at the police outpost, and mediation settled the dispute. He was then called to the outpost for questioning on 5 November.\nThe complaint asks for the outpost's CCTV footage, station diary and medical reports to be examined, and for the officer's transfer order to be verified.\nSenior police officers are inquiring into the complaint. Shirur Police Inspector Vinod Patil said the matter is under investigation.","i":"illustration-e267bbb359","a":["Shirur","Shirur taluka","Shirur town","Ghodnadi"]},{"u":"pune/mahalunge-maharera-rejects-godrej-hill-retreat-2-developer-forfeit-bid.html","h":"Mahalunge: MahaRERA rejects Godrej Hill Retreat 2 developer's bid to forfeit 1%, orders ₹7.92 lakh refund","s":"MahaRERA found that Mahalunge Township Developers LLP wrongly calculated a cancellation period in a dispute over Flat No. 0101 in Tower B5 of Godrej Hill Retreat 2.","k":"Mahalunge","c":"Business","t":"2026-11-12T18:46:12+05:30","g":["Godrej Hill Retreat 2","Mahalunge","Homebuyer refund"],"b":"Mahalunge Township Developers LLP, the developer of Godrej Hill Retreat 2 in Mahalunge, has failed in its bid to forfeit 1% of a homebuyer's payment. The Maharashtra Real Estate Regulatory Authority (MahaRERA) rejected the attempt to deduct 1% and ordered the refund of the entire ₹7.92 lakh.\nThe dispute concerned Flat No. 0101 in Tower B5 of the project, which is registered under MahaRERA number P52100049435. The buyer's booking was confirmed on July 2, 2024, and the formal allotment letter was issued on July 15. Facing financial constraints, he requested cancellation on July 20, five days after receiving the allotment letter.\nThe developer acknowledged the request but did not return the money. Emails sent in September 2024 said the refund was under approval, with no payment timeline.\nIt argued that the cancellation period should run from July 2, when the booking was confirmed, and that it was entitled to deduct 1% before returning the balance. MahaRERA found that the developer had wrongly calculated the cancellation period from the earlier booking confirmation, not from the formal allotment letter.","i":"illustration-749584ebe6","a":[]},{"u":"pune/chikhali-spine-road-murder-case-cracked-police-trace-accused.html","h":"Chikhali Spine Road murder case cracked, police trace the accused","s":"Police found important clues in investigating the murder of a young man whose body was hidden in bushes, and have traced those accused.","k":"Pimpri-Chinchwad","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-12T17:55:18+05:30","g":["Chikhali Spine Road","Murder case","Pimpri-Chinchwad"],"b":"Police have cracked the murder case of a young man whose body was found hidden in the bushes along Chikhali Spine Road in Pimpri-Chinchwad, and have traced the accused.\nThe discovery of the body caused alarm across the area. In their investigation, police found important clues.","i":"illustration-fb3b10a3eb","a":["Chikhali","Chikhli"]},{"u":"pune/cancer-patient-arrested-fake-hijack-threat-air-india-flight-kolkata-mumbai.html","h":"Cancer patient, 56, arrested for fake hijack threat on Air India flight from Kolkata to Mumbai","s":"A 56-year-old cancer patient was handed over to the NSCBI Airport Police Station, under Bidhannagar City Police, by CISF personnel who took him into custody on suspicion.","k":"Air India flight","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-12T17:13:02+05:30","g":["Air India","Kolkata","Hijack threat"],"b":"On November 10, a note warning of a hijack was found in one of the aircraft's toilets at Netaji Subhash Chandra Bose International Airport in Kolkata, and a 56-year-old cancer patient has been arrested for the fake threat.\nThe note was found as the plane, on the Air India flight from Kolkata to Mumbai, was getting ready for takeoff. A passenger brought the note to notice and the pilot alerted Air Traffic Control.\nThe plane was moved to an isolation bay, and security agencies searched it thoroughly. The threat was found to be a hoax; the flight was delayed by seven hours.\nCISF personnel took the man into custody on suspicion and handed him over to the NSCBI Airport Police Station, under Bidhannagar City Police. During questioning, he confessed. Police say both he and his wife are suffering from cancer.\nHe had to travel to Mumbai and then to Africa for work, and did not want to leave his wife alone in Kolkata. He told police he planted the note while in distress.\nA senior Bidhannagar City Police official said they understand his emotional situation, but the act is a serious offence that troubled many passengers, and legal action will follow.","i":"illustration-5d12d55274","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pcmc-orders-free-flats-8-of-9-moshi-garbage-depot-tragedy-victims.html","h":"PCMC orders free flats at Yashwantnagar for families of 8 of 9 Moshi garbage depot tragedy victims","s":"Dr. Vijay Suryawanshi, Municipal Commissioner of PCMC, signed an order allotting free flats to eight families; the heirs of one employee have yet to complete their documentation.","k":"Moshi garbage depot tragedy","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-12T17:02:21+05:30","g":["PCMC","Moshi garbage depot tragedy","Yashwantnagar"],"b":"Free flats from the civic body’s stock in the Slum Rehabilitation Authority (SRA) project at Yashwantnagar, Pimpri, have been ordered by the Pimpri Chinchwad Municipal Corporation (PCMC) for the families of eight of the nine civic employees who died in the Moshi garbage depot tragedy on July 8.\nMunicipal Commissioner Dr. Vijay Suryawanshi signed the allotment order, which follows a proposal approved on November 5, 2026. Once the families complete the required administrative formalities, they will receive possession.\nPCMC had earlier sanctioned and distributed ₹10 lakh to the legal heirs of each deceased employee.\nThe ninth family is not yet covered, because the heirs have not finished their documentation. The administration said the process to allot a flat to that family will begin once the paperwork is complete.\nDeputy Commissioner Anna Bodade said that for now, allotment orders for 8 flats have been issued, as the heirs of one employee have yet to complete the necessary documentation.\n“The Municipal Corporation is sensitive to the need for providing both financial assistance and a rightful place to live,”\nDr. Suryawanshi said","i":"illustration-1e9cfc99ef","a":["Moshi"]},{"u":"pune/pune-bomb-threat-email-targets-pmc-airport-jalsa.html","h":"Bomb threat email targets PMC headquarters, Pune airport and Amitabh Bachchan’s Jalsa","s":"An email that threatens explosions at Pune airport and the Pune Municipal Corporation headquarters mentions a group calling itself the ‘Khalistan National Army’, and neither the sender’s identity nor any genuine connection with that organisation is verified.","k":"Bomb threat email","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-12T16:51:42+05:30","g":["Bomb threat","PMC","Pune airport","Amitabh Bachchan","Diljit Dosanjh"],"b":"A bomb threat email that targets the Pune Municipal Corporation (PMC) headquarters, Pune airport, Amitabh Bachchan’s Jalsa and a Diljit Dosanjh concert was, according to the email, sent to email addresses associated with the PMC at 1:16 pm on Thursday, November 12, 2026.\nThe sender threatened to carry out a bomb explosion at the PMC headquarters and the Mayor’s Office at 3:11 pm, and threatened explosions at Pune airport later in the night. The email also has references to several locations in Mumbai.\nThe message mentions Amitabh Bachchan’s Jalsa bungalow in Juhu, Mumbai, and warns of an attack on the property. It also refers to a Diljit Dosanjh concert scheduled for November 27 in Mumbai’s Mahalaxmi area, threatening an explosion and warning people against attending the event.\nThe email refers to a group identifying itself as the ‘Khalistan National Army’ and includes the names of certain individuals. The identity of the sender, and any genuine connection with that organisation, remain unverified.\nThis is not the first time the PMC has been named in a bomb threat. On November 2, the PMC headquarters and Mayor’s Office were said to have received similar threats, and police and bomb detection teams conducted security checks.","i":"","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pune-two-dead-car-rams-parked-container-wadki.html","h":"Two dead as car rams parked container at Wadki on Pune-Saswad road","s":"Fursungi police have registered a case against an unidentified driver of a Haryana-registered container that a car hit at Wadki, where two people in the car died.","k":"Wadki","c":"Accidents and fires","t":"2026-11-12T16:39:05+05:30","g":["Pune","Wadki","Pune-Saswad road","Fursungi police"],"b":"Two people in a car are dead after it rams, from behind, a container parked in the dark on a service road at Wadki on the Pune-Saswad road, at around 12:15 am on Tuesday.\nThe crash happened near Dahava Mail (the tenth mile). The driver of the car suffered minor injuries.\nPolice say the driver of the Haryana-registered container had parked it on the service road heading towards Hadapsar, where parking is not allowed. The parking lights were off and there were no safety measures behind it, police say.\nThe container driver left the spot after the crash and has not been identified.\nFursungi police have registered a case against the container driver under various sections of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita and the Motor Vehicles Act. Police Sub-Inspector Santosh More is investigating.","i":"","a":["Saswad"]},{"u":"pune/wellington-team-india-flight-narrowly-averts-major-accident-severe-turbulence.html","h":"Wellington: Team India flight narrowly averts major accident, circles 26 minutes in severe turbulence","s":"Pilots of an Air New Zealand flight carrying members of India's Test team to Wellington made a go-around in gusting wind and landed safely, with no one injured.","k":"Team India","c":"City","t":"2026-11-12T15:33:06+05:30","g":["Team India","Shubman Gill","KL Rahul","Wellington"],"b":"Air New Zealand flight NZ5817, which left Hamilton for Wellington with eight to 10 members of India's Test team on board, had to abort its first landing in gusting wind at around 12:45 pm, made a go-around, and landed safely at 1:06 pm.\nTeam India's flight narrowly escaped a major accident in Wellington after circling for 26 minutes in severe turbulence.\nIndia's Test squad members on board included Shubman Gill, KL Rahul, Anshul Kamboj and bowling coach Morne Morkel, along with support staff. They were flying to Wellington to prepare for the Test series when strong winds made their first landing attempt fail.\nThe plane left Hamilton at 11:43 am local time. As it neared Wellington airport, the wind picked up sharply and the aircraft faced strong crosswinds and turbulence that briefly upset its balance.\nAt around 12:45 pm, with the plane only a few hundred feet above the runway, the pilots had to abort the landing in the gusting wind. They took the plane back up to more than 5,000 feet.\nThe pilots tried again once the wind eased slightly, after circling. The plane landed safely at 1:06 pm, 26 minutes behind schedule. No one was injured.\nThe Test series between India and New Zealand begins on 19 November, with the first Test at Wellington's Basin Reserve.","i":"illustration-3b6f3eb423","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pune-bhosari-gaothan-water-tank-overflows-nearly-hour.html","h":"Bhosari Gaothan water tank overflows for nearly an hour, thousands of litres said to be wasted","s":"A Bhosari Gaothan water tank overflowed for nearly an hour at a time when Pimpri-Chinchwad is facing water shortages.","k":"Bhosari Gaothan","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-12T15:22:34+05:30","g":["Bhosari Gaothan","Pimpri-Chinchwad","Water shortages","Water tank"],"b":"Thousands of litres of water are said to have been wasted when a water tank in Shantinagar, Bhosari Gaothan, overflowed for nearly an hour on Wednesday midnight.\nResidents expressed anger on finding that the staff member concerned was not present at the site. The water supply was eventually stopped following complaints from locals.\nCitizens have demanded action against the staff responsible and questioned the civic body's monitoring of water storage facilities.","i":"illustration-ebe528b95b","a":["Bhosari"]},{"u":"pune/swargate-police-recover-50-tolas-dowry-gold-hunt-sister-in-law-continues.html","h":"Swargate police recover all 50 tolas of dowry gold in woman's suicide case; hunt for sister-in-law continues","s":"In a woman's suicide case, Swargate police have recovered all 50 tolas of gold, and the hunt for her sister-in-law, a fourth accused, continues.","k":"Swargate dowry case","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-12T15:12:00+05:30","g":["Pune","Swargate","Dowry","Pune Police"],"b":"Swargate police have recovered all 50 tolas of gold allegedly given to her husband's family at the time of a woman's marriage, in a case of her suicide that followed alleged harassment over dowry demands.\nThe case was registered at Swargate Police Station on allegations that her husband and in-laws subjected her to physical and mental harassment over dowry demands.\nYashwant Nikam, Senior Police Inspector of Swargate Police Station, said the entire 50 tolas of gold had been recovered.\nHer husband, father-in-law and mother-in-law have been arrested. Earlier, police had sought an extension of the trio's police custody to recover the remaining 15 tolas of gold, seize the mother-in-law's mobile phone allegedly used in connection with the dowry demands and trace the sister-in-law, and the court granted it.\nWith the recovery complete, police are now preparing to produce the three before the court and seek their magisterial custody.\nThe hunt for her sister-in-law, the fourth accused, continues: she remains absconding. Investigators have traced her last known location to her residence and are making efforts to locate and arrest her.\nPolice are also gathering further evidence, including details of the alleged demands for gold ornaments and other valuables, chat records and call details.","i":"illustration-f04b162674","a":["Swargate"]},{"u":"pune/mns-swimming-protest-mutha-right-canal-punekars-water-cuts.html","h":"MNS takes a dip at Mutha Right Canal in symbolic protest as Punekars face water cuts","s":"The Maharashtra Navnirman Sena (MNS) swam in the Mutha Right Canal to protest the water cuts Punekars face.","k":"Parvati","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-12T15:00:48+05:30","g":["MNS","Mutha Right Canal","Parvati","Water cuts","Pune"],"b":"In a symbolic swimming protest, the Maharashtra Navnirman Sena (MNS) took a dip in the Mutha Right Canal near Janata Vasahat in Parvati as Pune faces the possibility of alternate-day water supply.\nPunekars face water cuts, and the dip in the canal was MNS's protest.","i":"","a":["Parvati","Parvati Paytha","Parvati Gaon","Parvati Darshan"]},{"u":"pune/kolwadi-man-allegedly-beaten-to-death-by-in-laws.html","h":"Kolwadi: man allegedly beaten to death by in-laws; case portrayed as road accident","s":"Two men arrested over a 24-year-old man's death at Kolwadi in Pune district confessed in questioning to assaulting him, police say; police have also seized a wooden stick allegedly used in an attack on him.","k":"Kolwadi","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-12T14:49:52+05:30","g":["Kolwadi","Lonikand Police","Pune"],"b":"A 24-year-old man was allegedly beaten to death at Kolwadi in Pune district by his father-in-law and great-grandfather-in-law, whom Lonikand Police have arrested. Police say the case was initially portrayed as a road accident.\nAccording to police, the 24-year-old had gone to his in-laws’ house on 9 November while searching for his wife after a family dispute. The two men allegedly assaulted him with a wooden stick, leading to his death.\nThe accused allegedly claimed he had died after falling from his two-wheeler. However, police found no signs of an accident at the spot.\nDuring questioning, the accused confessed to the assault, police say. Police have also seized the wooden stick allegedly used in the attack. Further investigation is underway.","i":"illustration-b9fc725db2","a":["Lonikand"]},{"u":"pune/pune-thergaon-watch-shop-burglary-wakad-police-arrest-two.html","h":"Thergaon watch shop burglary: Wakad Police arrest two, recover stolen goods worth ₹9.84 lakh","s":"Two men have been arrested over a Thergaon watch shop burglary, 108 high-end watches have been recovered, and police say the stolen property has been recovered in full.","k":"Thergaon burglary","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-12T14:32:53+05:30","g":["Thergaon","Wakad Police","Burglary","Pune"],"b":"Wakad Police arrested two men for the burglary of a watch shop near Dange Chowk in Thergaon, which took place between 9 pm on November 3 and 10 am on November 4, and recovered stolen goods worth ₹9.84 lakh.\nThe thieves got in by prying open the roof sheets and breaking through the plaster of Paris (POP) ceiling. They took watches and the shop's DVR machine, which police valued at ₹8,23,701.\nWith the CCTV recorder gone, the investigation team went through footage from 150 to 200 government and private CCTV cameras around the spot. The team worked out the route the suspect took while fleeing on an Activa two-wheeler with a companion.\nAssistant Police Inspector Shrinivas Darade and his Crime Detection Team set a trap and caught one of the accused on November 10. Police say he confessed during questioning and named his accomplice, who was arrested the same day at 10.40 pm.\nDuring their police custody, police recovered 108 high-end watches from brands including Titan, Titan Raga, Titan Edge and Fastrack, valued at ₹9,04,770. They also seized the Activa, valued at ₹50,000, and a mobile phone, valued at ₹30,000. Police say the stolen property has been recovered in full.\nA case (Crime Register No. 807/2026) was registered at Wakad Police Station on the shop owner's complaint under Sections 305, 331(3), 331(4) and 3(5) of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023. Senior Police Inspector Vitthal Salunkhe directed the investigation, and API Darade is continuing it.","i":"","a":["Thergaon"]},{"u":"pune/pmc-proposes-two-underground-paatal-lok-tunnels-31-km.html","h":"PMC proposes two underground ‘Paatal Lok’ tunnels, 31 km in all, to ease Pune’s traffic","s":"The Pune Municipal Corporation’s plan for two tunnels, one of 23 km and one of 8 km, is still at the planning stage.","k":"Paatal Lok","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-12T14:22:21+05:30","g":["Paatal Lok","Pune Municipal Corporation","Underground tunnels","Pune traffic"],"b":"The Pune Municipal Corporation (PMC) proposes two underground tunnels, linking Bhosari with Undri and Bhugaon with Erandwane, to ease Pune’s traffic congestion.\nThe tunnels, 31 km in all, come under its ‘Paatal Lok’ project. The Bhosari–Undri tunnel is 23 km long and the Bhugaon–Erandwane tunnel is 8 km long.\nThe civic body has approved the process of appointing expert consultants to prepare Detailed Project Reports (DPRs) for the tunnels.\nThe project is still at the planning stage. Further feasibility studies and approvals are required before construction can begin.","i":"illustration-4f202670bb","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pimpri-chinchwad-cyber-fraud-network-alleged-dubai-bangkok-china-links.html","h":"Pimpri-Chinchwad Cyber Police probe fraud network with alleged Dubai, Bangkok, China links","s":"More than 150 bank accounts linked to a suspected cyber fraud network are under investigation, and money from online scams was allegedly sent abroad through hawala and cryptocurrency.","k":"Pimpri-Chinchwad","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-12T14:11:49+05:30","g":["Cyber fraud","Pimpri-Chinchwad","Cyber Police","Pune"],"b":"Police arrested a 26-year-old man from Nigdi on 2 November, and Pimpri-Chinchwad Cyber Police are probing an international cyber fraud network with alleged links to Dubai, Bangkok and China.\nTwo other accused, from Chikhali and Akurdi, were arrested along with him. Money collected through online scams was allegedly transferred abroad using hawala and cryptocurrency channels.\nThe suspected network is linked to more than 150 bank accounts, which are now under investigation.\nThe probe continues as police work to trace the international money trail and identify others involved.","i":"illustration-da8b0f6335","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pune-priyanka-chopra-mother-brother-sell-koregaon-park-bungalow.html","h":"Priyanka Chopra’s mother and brother to sell Koregaon Park bungalow for ₹6.5 crore","s":"Real estate firm Suroj Buildcon has bought the Koregaon Park bungalow of Madhu Chopra and Siddharth Chopra, according to property registration documents.","k":"Koregaon Park","c":"Business","t":"2026-11-12T14:01:15+05:30","g":["Koregaon Park","Priyanka Chopra","Suroj Buildcon","Real estate"],"b":"Madhu Chopra and Siddharth Chopra, mother and brother of actor Priyanka Chopra Jonas, have agreed to sell their Koregaon Park bungalow for ₹6.5 crore, and the sale agreement was registered on October 21, 2026.\nThe property has been sold to real estate firm Suroj Buildcon, according to property registration documents. The bungalow is in Liberty Co-operative Housing Society on North Main Road in Ghorpadi village.\nThe transaction involved a stamp duty payment of ₹45.5 lakh and registration charges of ₹30,000.\nThe 3,754 sq ft plot has a ground-floor built-up area of 2,180 sq ft, a 950 sq ft basement, a 2,232 sq ft garden and a 400 sq ft parking area.\nIn March 2024, the family had given the bungalow on leave and licence to The Urban Nomads Community Pvt Ltd, a co-living and co-working company. The monthly rent was ₹2.06 lakh, with a security deposit of ₹6 lakh.\nThe family also bought another 4,800 sq ft property in Koregaon Park in August 2017 for ₹5.6 crore. It was leased out in February 2025 for ₹2.25 lakh a month under a five-year agreement.","i":"","a":["Koregaon Park","KP","Koregaon Park Annexe"]},{"u":"pune/star-air-passenger-slams-repeated-rescheduling-last-minute-cancellation.html","h":"Passenger slams Star Air over repeated rescheduling, last-minute cancellation of Pune–Nanded flight","s":"A Star Air passenger questions the airline's lack of accountability after a Pune–Nanded flight's cancellation.","k":"Star Air flight","c":"City","t":"2026-11-12T13:50:39+05:30","g":["Star Air","Nanded","Flight rescheduling","Flight cancellation"],"b":"A Pune–Nanded flight that had been rescheduled four times was cancelled at the last minute, and a passenger slams Star Air over it.\nAccording to the passenger, the flight was originally scheduled to depart from Nanded at 9:30 AM and was rescheduled several times before passengers were told around 10 AM that it had been cancelled. Passengers were then told another flight would arrive at 5:30 PM, with no assurance that it would operate as scheduled.\nThe passenger says tickets for 3–4 people were booked nearly a month in advance.\nThe passenger questioned the airline's lack of accountability and criticised the administration for failing to address such issues. Passengers should not be made to suffer despite booking tickets well in advance, the passenger said.","i":"","a":[]},{"u":"pune/maharera-orders-jairaj-realty-pay-buyer-interest-maha-trade-market-delay.html","h":"MahaRERA orders Jairaj Realty to pay buyer interest over Maha Trade Market delay","s":"A Maha Trade Market Phase-1 buyer who booked a commercial unit for ₹50.24 lakh and paid ₹33.39 lakh including taxes alleged being left waiting for possession, and MahaRERA rejected Jairaj Realty's payment-default defence.","k":"Maha Trade Market","c":"Business","t":"2026-11-12T13:23:06+05:30","g":["Jairaj Realty","Maha Trade Market","Maharashtra Real Estate Regulatory Authority"],"b":"Jairaj Realty LLP must pay delayed-possession interest to a buyer of a commercial unit in its Maha Trade Market Phase-1 project, the Maharashtra Real Estate Regulatory Authority (MahaRERA) has ordered. It held that the developer had failed to deliver possession of Unit B1.012 within the agreed deadline.\nThe buyer had booked the unit for ₹50.24 lakh through an agreement executed on March 18, 2020. Possession was promised by December 31, 2024, and a six-month grace period extended the deadline to June 30, 2025. MahaRERA held that the occupancy certificate, which is mandatory, was also not delivered within the agreed deadline.\nThe buyer, who had paid ₹33.39 lakh including taxes, alleged that he was left waiting for possession without any clear construction schedule, even after repeated follow-ups.\nJairaj Realty argued that the buyer had defaulted on payments, claiming nearly ₹7 lakh remained outstanding, and also blamed the COVID-19 pandemic for construction delays. MahaRERA rejected the developer's attempt to blame the delay on alleged payment defaults by the purchaser, observing that the demand notices the developer cited had been issued only after the contractual possession deadline had already expired.\nThe Authority directed Jairaj Realty to pay interest on the amount received towards the unit cost.","i":"illustration-b779ea023e","a":[]},{"u":"pune/viman-nagar-shawarma-owner-booked-gas-cylinder-bhatti-outside-shop.html","h":"Viman Nagar shawarma owner booked over gas cylinder, bhatti outside shop","s":"A 25-year-old shawarma shop owner in Viman Nagar has been booked over a gas cylinder and bhatti placed outside his shop.","k":"Viman Nagar","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-12T13:12:32+05:30","g":["Viman Nagar","Vimantal police","Gas cylinder","Pune"],"b":"Harshal Tukaram Marathe, 25, owner of King’s Shawarma at Shop No. 03, Niko Garden, Viman Nagar, has been booked by Vimantal (Airport) police for cooking on a gas cylinder and bhatti outside his shop. FIR No. 546/2026 was registered on 12 November 2026.\nHe was booked under section 287 of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023, for negligent conduct with an inflammable substance.\nAccording to the FIR, a constable and Police Amaldar Puttewad of Vimantal police station, on night patrol, reached Niko Garden at about 12:50 am on 12 November. The FIR says they found an inflammable gas cylinder connected to a stove, and a bhatti, placed outside the shop near the gate, with food being cooked as customers stood beside it, and that the business was being run in a way that could endanger the lives of people passing by.\nThe constable lodged the complaint on behalf of the government. Inspector Govind Sayaji Jadhav registered the FIR, and PSI Dhananjay Bhujang Gade is investigating.","i":"illustration-2efe8c3114","a":["Viman Nagar","Vimantal"]},{"u":"pune/yerawada-man-71-loses-22-lakh-digital-arrest-fraud.html","h":"Yerawada man, 71, loses ₹22 lakh in ‘digital arrest’ fraud","s":"Vishrantwadi police are investigating the loss of ₹22 lakh by a retired Yerawada man, 71, to callers who threatened him with “digital arrest”.","k":"Yerawada","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-12T13:02:01+05:30","g":["Pune","Yerawada","Digital arrest","Vishrantwadi police","Fraud"],"b":"A retired Yerawada man, 71, lost ₹22 lakh in a “digital arrest” fraud, transferring the money in two payments between 12 and 15 October to bank accounts named by callers posing as police and CBI officers.\nThe callers threatened him with “digital arrest”, said he would be arrested unless he paid money for “digital verification” of his accounts, and asked for a ₹40 lakh “security deposit”.\nAccording to the FIR, a WhatsApp caller who called himself “Vijay Sharma” of the telephone department’s Delhi office told the complainant on 5 October that a SIM card in his name was being used to send obscene messages and photos to girls.\nA man calling himself “Inspector Ajay Patil” of a Karnataka police station then joined the call and said his superior “Manoj” was on leave. Later a “CBI officer Jay Shankar” joined, who claimed he was linked to a ₹3-crore fraud through a new Canara Bank account and to a “Sadakat Khan” who was doing child trafficking.\nHe paid from his Punjab National Bank accounts, partly with a loan taken against his gold. The callers later stopped responding to his messages.\nHe complained on the NCRB portal and to the cyber police on 5 November.\nVishrantwadi police have registered a case (FIR 0561/2026) against unknown persons under BNS sections 318(4) and 319(2) and section 66(D) of the IT Act. Police Inspector Rajendra Panhale of Vishrantwadi police station registered the case on 11 November and has taken up the investigation.","i":"illustration-5d2807adbc","a":["Yerawada","Yerwada","Yeravda","Yerawda","Yerwda"]},{"u":"pune/uruli-kanchan-three-men-face-atrocity-case-dalit-woman-alleged-molested.html","h":"Uruli Kanchan: Three men face atrocity case after Dalit woman alleged she was molested, abused, threatened","s":"A case against three men from Peth in Haveli taluka is registered at the Uruli Kanchan Police Station, and Sub-Divisional Police Officer Bapurao Dadas is investigating.","k":"Uruli Kanchan","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-12T12:51:30+05:30","g":["Uruli Kanchan","Haveli","Atrocity case","Dalit woman"],"b":"Three men from Peth in Haveli taluka face an atrocity case in Uruli Kanchan after a Dalit woman alleged that she was molested, and that she and her son were abused over their caste and threatened with death, in the Peth area on Sunday, November 8, around 7.30 pm.\nShe had gone to a relative's house over a dispute involving her son. One of the men allegedly began an argument, saying her son had used abusive language over the phone. Another then allegedly rushed at her, abused her and outraged her modesty by pulling at her pallu, the end of her saree.\nThe third man arrived later and also abused the woman and her son, the complaint says. She has alleged that the three made derogatory remarks about her caste, told her she could no longer live in the village, and threatened to cut off her son's legs.\nPolice have registered the case under the Scheduled Castes and the Scheduled Tribes (Prevention of Atrocities) Act and other sections, at the Uruli Kanchan Police Station. Sub-Divisional Police Officer Bapurao Dadas is investigating. There is no information yet on any arrests.","i":"illustration-5a31ba0eca","a":["Uruli Kanchan","Haveli","Haveli taluka","Haveli tehsil"]},{"u":"pune/pune-thieves-steal-gold-cash-64-lakh-homes-seven-areas-lakshmi-puja.html","h":"Pune: thieves steal gold, cash worth approximately ₹64 lakh from homes in seven areas during Lakshmi Puja","s":"The biggest theft from Pune homes during Lakshmi Puja, at a Hadapsar bungalow, took gold ornaments and cash worth ₹47 lakh in all, and Hadapsar police are investigating.","k":"Lakshmi Puja thefts","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-12T11:53:45+05:30","g":["Lakshmi Puja","Hadapsar","Thefts","Hadapsar police"],"b":"Homes in Hadapsar, Katraj, Mohammadwadi, Ashtapur, Bibvewadi, Kondhwa and Kalepadal, seven areas of Pune, were targeted during Lakshmi Puja, and thieves stole gold and cash worth approximately ₹64 lakh from them. Valuables kept in prayer rooms for the puja were stolen.\nIn Hadapsar, the biggest theft took gold ornaments and ₹12 lakh in cash, worth ₹47 lakh in all, from a bungalow, where the family had kept the valuables in the prayer room for Lakshmi Puja. Around midnight, the thieves allegedly entered through a sliding glass panel.\nA flat in Katraj's Santoshnagar lost valuables worth ₹1.68 lakh, and gold and cash worth ₹3.28 lakh were stolen in Bibvewadi's Sukhsagarnagar. Gold, ₹50,000 in cash, a two-wheeler and a car key worth ₹2.65 lakh were taken in Ashtapur.\nGold ornaments worth ₹1.82 lakh were stolen from a prayer room in Kondhwa's Dr Babasaheb Ambedkar Nagar, and a senior citizen lodged the complaint. Two more thefts in Kalepadal involved gold ornaments worth ₹1.82 lakh and jewellery worth ₹7.34 lakh, the latter on Mohammadwadi Road.\nHadapsar police are investigating the bungalow theft, and PSI Shubham Shinde is the investigating officer. Ambegaon and Bharati Vidyapeeth police are investigating the Katraj and Bibvewadi thefts. Cases have been registered at Lonikand police station for Ashtapur and at Kalepadal police station.","i":"illustration-870e9e3c51","a":["Hadapsar"]},{"u":"pune/pune-tempo-carrying-paper-catches-fire-juna-bazaar-mangalwar-peth.html","h":"Tempo carrying paper catches fire in Juna Bazaar, Mangalwar Peth after firecracker lands on it","s":"Pune Fire Brigade personnel brought under control a fire that broke out on a paper-laden tempo after a firecracker landed on it.","k":"Mangalwar Peth","c":"Accidents and fires","t":"2026-11-12T00:40:57+05:30","g":["Mangalwar Peth","Juna Bazaar","Pune Fire Brigade","Tempo fire"],"b":"A firecracker landed on a tempo carrying paper and other materials in the Juna Bazaar area of Mangalwar Peth, and the tempo caught fire.\nPune Fire Brigade personnel rushed to the spot and brought the fire under control. No injuries were reported.","i":"","a":["Mangalwar Peth","Mangalvar Peth","Mangalwar Pet"]},{"u":"pune/pune-shivajinagar-gaothan-fire-breaks-out-seventh-floor-flat-balcony.html","h":"Shivajinagar Gaothan: fire breaks out on balcony of seventh-floor flat, no injuries reported","s":"Pune Fire Brigade personnel sprayed water from outside into the balcony of a locked seventh-floor flat in Shivajinagar Gaothan, and no injuries have been reported.","k":"Shivajinagar Gaothan","c":"Accidents and fires","t":"2026-11-12T00:29:58+05:30","g":["Pune Fire Brigade","Shivajinagar Gaothan","Gulab Sadan","Pune"],"b":"A fire broke out on a seventh-floor flat's balcony at Gulab Sadan, near Rokdoba Temple in Shivajinagar Gaothan, Pune, and Pune Fire Brigade personnel put it out.\nAs the flat was locked, the personnel sprayed water into the balcony from outside with a fire hose.\nA small bicycle, clothes, notebooks and books were damaged. No injuries have been reported.","i":"","a":["Shivajinagar","Shivajinagar Gaothan"]},{"u":"pune/journalists-allegedly-manhandled-emraan-hashmi-gunmaster-trailer-launch-kothrud.html","h":"Journalists allegedly manhandled at Emraan Hashmi’s ‘Gunmaster’ trailer launch in Kothrud","s":"Some members of the production team of Emraan Hashmi’s upcoming film ‘Gunmaster’ allegedly misbehaved with journalists at its trailer launch, and the actor’s management team allegedly escorted him into his car and left the venue.","k":"Kothrud","c":"City","t":"2026-11-11T23:53:53+05:30","g":["Emraan Hashmi","Gunmaster","Kothrud","Journalists"],"b":"Journalists were allegedly manhandled at the trailer launch of actor Emraan Hashmi’s upcoming film ‘Gunmaster’ at City Pride Theatre in Kothrud, Pune. Some members of the film’s production team, who had come from Mumbai, allegedly misbehaved with them.\nA few journalists who questioned the team members’ conduct were allegedly pushed around. The incident triggered anger and strong resentment among the media fraternity.\nJournalists tried to bring the incident to Emraan Hashmi’s attention and seek his reaction. Before he could respond, his management team allegedly escorted him into his car and left the venue.","i":"","a":["Kothrud"]},{"u":"pune/pune-tilak-road-bpcl-pump-allegedly-refused-regular-petrol.html","h":"Tilak Road BPCL pump refused regular petrol, customer alleges","s":"A customer's complaint to the Ministry of Petroleum and Natural Gas seeks an immediate investigation into the conduct of staff at a BPCL pump on Tilak Road.","k":"Tilak Road","c":"City","t":"2026-11-11T21:06:04+05:30","g":["BPCL","Tilak Road","Swargate","Regular petrol"],"b":"A customer alleges that a BPCL petrol pump on Tilak Road near Swargate refused regular petrol despite a specific request, and has lodged a formal complaint with the Ministry of Petroleum and Natural Gas.\nThe complaint is against the Bharat Petroleum (BPCL) outlet, and the customer has submitted video evidence of the incident.\nIt seeks an immediate investigation into the staff's conduct and verification of fuel availability. It also seeks strict action if the allegations are established.\nIt also raises concerns over possible pressure on customers to buy premium fuel rather than their preferred regular petrol. The customer has sought from BPCL a written clarification on the right of consumers to choose their preferred fuel category.","i":"","a":["Swargate"]},{"u":"pune/inflation-jolt-this-diwali-amul-mother-dairy-milk-prices.html","h":"Inflation jolt this Diwali: Amul milk prices up after Mother Dairy, from 12 November","s":"Amul Gold goes from ₹70 to ₹74 a litre, and Mother Dairy, a major milk supplier in Delhi-NCR, has put prices up by ₹2 to ₹4 a litre.","k":"Milk prices","c":"Business","t":"2026-11-11T20:33:33+05:30","g":["Milk prices","Amul","Mother Dairy","Inflation"],"b":"Amul has decided to raise its milk prices from 12 November 2026, after Mother Dairy, it has emerged: an inflation jolt this Diwali.\nAmul Gold costs ₹4 a litre more, going from ₹70 to ₹74. Amul Taaza and Amul Fresh are each said to go up by ₹2 a litre.\nMother Dairy, a major milk supplier in Delhi-NCR, has already raised its prices by ₹2 to ₹4 a litre for both loose and packaged liquid milk, also from 12 November.\nThe companies are said to have raised prices because producing and distributing milk now costs more: green and dry fodder, cattle feed, packaging and transport all cost more.\nHouseholds that buy milk every day are likely to see their monthly budget go up, from the daily tea and coffee to other needs at home.","i":"illustration-c57e0d9b0e","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pune-major-pipeline-burst-near-nigdi-wastes-lakhs-litres-water.html","h":"Major pipeline burst near Nigdi wastes lakhs of litres of water","s":"Lakhs of litres of potable water were lost, and traffic was disrupted at Nigdi Chowk.","k":"Nigdi pipeline burst","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-11T19:52:56+05:30","g":["Nigdi","Pimpri-to-Nigdi Metro extension","water pipeline"],"b":"A major water pipeline burst near Nigdi, wasting lakhs of litres of potable water. The burst was on the stretch of the ongoing Pimpri-to-Nigdi Metro extension line.\nAt Nigdi Chowk, water spread across the road, disrupting traffic.","i":"","a":["Nigdi","Nigdi Pradhikaran","Pradhikaran"]},{"u":"pune/plus-valley-dangerous-shortcut-20-year-old-dies-in-200-metre-gorge.html","h":"Plus Valley: dangerous shortcut, 20-year-old dies in 200-metre gorge","s":"Paud Police, SVRSS personnel and the Roha Rescue Team recovered the body of a 20-year-old who died in a gorge at Plus Valley, a tourist spot in Pune district.","k":"Plus Valley","c":"Accidents and fires","t":"2026-11-11T17:51:45+05:30","g":["Plus Valley","Mulshi","Paud Police","Rope rescue"],"b":"A 20-year-old who had gone to a tourist spot in Pune district with four friends died after he is said to have fallen nearly 200 metres into a gorge at Plus Valley in Mulshi taluka.\nThe fall took place near the Milkybar Waterfall.\nWhile returning, the group is said to have taken a dangerous shortcut instead of the regular route. While climbing a steep hillside, he is said to have lost his footing and fallen into the gorge.\nPaud Police, SVRSS personnel and the Roha Rescue Team recovered his body in a rope-rescue operation across difficult terrain.","i":"illustration-dacde7e8ed","a":["Mulshi","Mulshi taluka"]},{"u":"pune/pune-wanowrie-fda-destroys-93-kg-sweets-suspends-licences-karachi-sweets.html","h":"Wanowrie: FDA destroys 93 kg of sweets, suspends licences of two Karachi Sweets units","s":"The Food and Drug Administration has suspended the food licences of two Karachi Sweets units in Wanowrie, Pune, and sent samples of their sweets to a laboratory for testing.","k":"Wanowrie","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-11T17:09:42+05:30","g":["Pune","Wanowrie","FDA","Karachi Sweets"],"b":"FDA officials raided Maa Karachi Sweets Mart and Shree Mohan Karachi Sweets Mart, two Karachi Sweets manufacturing units in Pune’s Wanowrie area, and seized 93 kg of sweets that were destroyed on the spot.\nThe Food and Drug Administration (FDA) acted under its ‘Safe Food, Safe Maharashtra’ campaign. The seized stock, which included laddoos, boondi and barfi, was valued at about ₹50,860.\nAs an immediate measure, the food licences of both units have been suspended. Suspecting quality issues, the officials collected samples of the sweets and sent them to a laboratory for testing. Further action will depend on the laboratory test results.","i":"","a":["Wanowrie","Wanawadi","Wanwadi","Wanowri","Wanavdi"]},{"u":"pune/kothrud-notorious-criminal-killed-swords-sickles-cctv-surfaced.html","h":"Kothrud: notorious criminal killed with swords and sickles, CCTV of attack surfaced","s":"A history-sheeter, 27, was killed in a sword and sickle attack in Pune’s Kothrud, and police have detained suspects.","k":"Kothrud","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-11T16:53:43+05:30","g":["Pune","Kothrud","Kothrud Police","CCTV"],"b":"A 27-year-old man was killed over past enmity at around 9:30 pm on November 8 in the Sutardara locality of Kothrud, and CCTV of the attack has surfaced.\nThe man was allegedly intercepted and assaulted with swords, sickles, iron weapons and wooden sticks by a group of three to four attackers.\nKothrud Police personnel who were on patrol rushed the man to a hospital, but doctors declared him dead before he could be treated.\nHe was a history-sheeter, with several criminal cases registered against him. Police have detained suspects in connection with the case.","i":"","a":["Kothrud"]},{"u":"pune/charholi-budruk-residents-say-damaged-pipeline-wasting-water-flooding-road.html","h":"Charholi Budruk residents say damaged pipeline is wasting drinking water, flooding road daily","s":"Residents of Bhosale Vasti have demanded immediate pipeline repairs and proper drainage from the Pimpri-Chinchwad Municipal Corporation (PCMC), saying hundreds of complaints brought no effective action.","k":"Charholi Budruk","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-11T16:17:44+05:30","g":["Charholi Budruk","Bhosale Vasti","PCMC","Drinking water"],"b":"Residents of Bhosale Vasti in Charholi Budruk, Pune, say a damaged pipeline is wasting drinking water and flooding their road every day, and claim that hundreds of complaints to the authorities have brought no effective action.\nThey say the ageing main drinking water pipeline and its connected tap lines break repeatedly, causing frequent leakages and daily flooding of the road. They allege thousands of litres of drinking water go to waste daily.\nThe waterlogging, they say, has made daily commuting difficult, especially for pedestrians, whom passing vehicles often splash with dirty water.\nThey also point to deep potholes, the absence of a proper footpath and frequent accidents on the stretch. They raise concerns about sanitation, mosquito breeding and health risks from the stagnant water.\nThey have demanded immediate pipeline repairs, proper drainage and restoration of the road from the Pimpri-Chinchwad Municipal Corporation (PCMC). They say they pay their taxes regularly.","i":"","a":["Charholi Budruk","Charholi","Charoli Budruk","Charholi Bk"]},{"u":"pune/pune-tree-fire-near-mundhwa-crematorium-major-incident-averted.html","h":"Tree fire near Mundhwa Crematorium, major incident averted","s":"Firefighters and security personnel made coordinated efforts to bring a tree fire in Pune under control, and no injuries or property damage were reported.","k":"Mundhwa Crematorium","c":"Accidents and fires","t":"2026-11-11T16:06:46+05:30","g":["Mundhwa","Pune","Fire brigade"],"b":"A tree caught fire near the entrance of Mundhwa Crematorium in Pune on Tuesday night, and security guards on duty, who noticed the blaze, immediately alerted the fire brigade.\nFirefighters, along with security personnel, made coordinated efforts to bring the fire under control. Their prompt response prevented the fire from spreading further, and a major incident was averted.\nNo injuries or property damage were reported.","i":"","a":["Mundhwa","Mundhawa"]},{"u":"pune/junnar-man-dies-peth-ghat-accident-way-home-sister-nephew-bhaubeej.html","h":"Junnar man, 33, dies in Peth Ghat accident on way home with sister, nephew on Bhaubeej","s":"An unidentified vehicle allegedly rammed a bike from behind in Peth Ghat; a 33-year-old Junnar man died and his sister and nephew sustained minor injuries.","k":"Peth Ghat","c":"Accidents and fires","t":"2026-11-11T15:55:47+05:30","g":["Peth Ghat","Junnar","Pune-Nashik Highway","Road accident","Bhaubeej"],"b":"A resident of Warulwadi in Junnar, 33, died in a road accident at Peth Ghat on the Pune-Nashik Highway while returning home with his sister and nephew for Bhaubeej.\nHe had travelled to Khed to bring his sister and nephew home for the festival. While the three were returning on a two-wheeler, an unidentified vehicle allegedly rammed their bike from behind in Peth Ghat.\nHe suffered severe head injuries and died at the spot. His sister and nephew sustained minor injuries.\nHe had recently got married and was his parents’ only son. His death has left the family and the Warulwadi community mourning.","i":"illustration-187854edf4","a":["Junnar","Junnar taluka"]},{"u":"pune/anna-hazare-hits-back-sonia-gandhi-serious-allegation-covert-rss-bjp-support.html","h":"Anna Hazare hits back at serious allegation by Sonia Gandhi of covert RSS-BJP support","s":"Sonia Gandhi’s autobiography alleges that Anna Hazare’s ‘India Against Corruption’ movement had covert RSS-BJP support, and Hazare said he has no connection with any party.","k":"Anna Hazare","c":"Politics","t":"2026-11-11T15:44:05+05:30","g":["Anna Hazare","Sonia Gandhi","India Against Corruption","Lokpal"],"b":"Anna Hazare hits back at a serious allegation in the autobiography ‘Belonging: A Journey of Love’ by senior Congress leader Sonia Gandhi: that his ‘India Against Corruption’ movement had the covert support of the Rashtriya Swayamsevak Sangh (RSS) and the Bharatiya Janata Party (BJP).\nGandhi writes that the agitation built political pressure on the then Congress-led UPA government. She also claims that the opposition’s aim was to end the UPA government’s rule.\nAsked about the claim in the book, Hazare said:\n“A responsible person should speak responsibly. Otherwise one’s own worth falls. I have no connection with any party. Whatever I do, I do for the good of the country and of society.”\nAnna Hazare, asked about the claim in the book\nThe ‘India Against Corruption’ agitation, led by Hazare at Jantar Mantar in Delhi in 2011, demanded an effective Lokpal law and strict action against corruption.\nThousands of citizens took part. The UPA government led by then Prime Minister Manmohan Singh came under heavy political pressure from the agitation.","i":"","a":[]},{"u":"pune/baramati-four-arrested-alleged-illegal-stock-110-mephentermine-injections.html","h":"Baramati: Four arrested for alleged illegal stock of 110 mephentermine sulphate injections","s":"A police team found 25 vials each with three of four men and 35 with the fourth, and materials worth Rs 2.31 lakh in all were seized.","k":"Baramati","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-11T15:33:27+05:30","g":["Baramati","Baramati city police","Mephentermine sulphate injections","Diwali"],"b":"Baramati city police have seized 110 vials of mephentermine sulphate injections in a raid in the Market Yard area on Indapur Road, and four people have been arrested over the alleged illegal stock.\nThe raid came amid a crackdown on the alleged unauthorised storage of medicinal injections ahead of Diwali.\nPolice received information that four men were waiting behind a food stall near the ground adjoining the Bharat Ratna Dr Babasaheb Ambedkar Students’ Hostel, carrying the vials. A police team raided the spot and found 35 vials with one of the men and 25 vials each with the other three. In all, materials worth Rs 2.31 lakh were seized.\nThe stock was seized because the accused lacked the mandatory licence needed to sell the medicine. In May, one of the four was booked for allegedly possessing 100 such injections.\nA case has been registered by Baramati city police, who are working to identify the original supplier of the injections and the person who transported the stock.","i":"illustration-41b08c7b9a","a":["Baramati","Baramati city","Baramati taluka"]},{"u":"pune/pune-vishrantwadi-17-year-old-allegedly-attacked-with-koyta.html","h":"‘Why are you spreading rumours about me?’: 17-year-old allegedly attacked with koyta in Vishrantwadi","s":"Vishrantwadi Police have arrested a 19-year-old accused and taken five minors into custody in connection with an incident in which a group allegedly attacked a 17-year-old boy with a koyta, seriously injuring him.","k":"Vishrantwadi","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-11T15:22:45+05:30","g":["Pune","Vishrantwadi","Koyta","Vishrantwadi Police"],"b":"A group allegedly attacked a 17-year-old boy with a koyta in the Bhimnagar area of Pune’s Vishrantwadi around 10:30 pm on 8 November, leaving him seriously injured.\nAccording to the complaint, the accused confronted the teenager over rumours allegedly being spread about one of them, and the argument escalated. The injured teenager was rushed to Sassoon General Hospital for treatment.\nVishrantwadi Police have arrested a 19-year-old accused, and five minors have been taken into custody in connection with the incident. Further investigation is underway.","i":"illustration-bcb776ca63","a":["Vishrantwadi","Vishrantvadi"]},{"u":"pune/pune-camp-fda-suspends-pasteur-ice-cream-parlour-licence-hygiene-violations.html","h":"Pune Camp: FDA suspends licence of Pasteur Ice Cream Parlour over serious hygiene violations","s":"A Pune Camp ice cream parlour may not carry on any food-related business during the suspension of its food licence, the Food and Drug Administration has ordered.","k":"Pune Camp","c":"City","t":"2026-11-11T15:12:11+05:30","g":["Pune Camp","FDA","Food safety","MG Road"],"b":"Pasteur Ice Cream Parlour on MG Road, Pune Camp, had its food licence suspended with immediate effect on November 10 by the Food and Drug Administration (FDA), over serious hygiene violations.\nThe FDA took the action under the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006, as part of its ‘Safe Food Safe Maharashtra’ campaign. Food safety officer Satish Hake inspected the premises. Licensing authority N R Sarkate, designated officer of Circle 6, ordered the suspension until further orders.\nAccording to the FDA, the kitchen had rodent droppings beneath racks and freezers, along with cobwebs, dust and peeling wall surfaces. Fruits and other food items were stored alongside sanitisers and disinfectants. Food products in freezers carried no best-before dates.\nThe parlour allegedly held only a retailer’s licence, yet it was preparing and selling samosas, sandwiches, burgers, pizzas, pav bhaji and falooda. It also failed to produce water and food testing reports and FoSTaC training certificates for its employees. A mandatory display about free drinking water was missing.\nThe FDA has prohibited any food-related business during the suspension. Joint Commissioner of FDA Pune division Shrikant Karkale warned that any violation of the order would invite strict legal action.","i":"illustration-64f3102b96","a":["Pune Camp","Camp","Pune Cantonment area"]},{"u":"pune/alandi-woman-75-dies-fire-building-behind-sant-dnyaneshwar-temple.html","h":"Alandi: 75-year-old woman dies in fire at building behind Sant Dnyaneshwar Maharaj temple","s":"A 75-year-old woman died in a fire at a three-storey building in Alandi where two families lived, and another elderly woman was rescued.","k":"Alandi fire","c":"Accidents and fires","t":"2026-11-11T15:01:35+05:30","g":["Alandi","Fire","Diwali","Pune"],"b":"A 75-year-old woman died in a fire that broke out between 7.30pm and 7.45pm on Monday, Diwali, in a three-storey building behind the Sant Dnyaneshwar Maharaj temple in Alandi.\nThe building adjoins the Jain Sthanak temple, on the southern side of the Sant Dnyaneshwar temple’s darshan mandap. Two families lived in the premises, and another elderly woman was rescued.\nThe 75-year-old suffered severe burn injuries and died. She had first been taken to the Alandi rural hospital and was later shifted to YCM Hospital in Pimpri.\nOfficials said a large quantity of cardboard stored on the first floor added to the spread of smoke. They said the building’s few windows and entrances made rescue difficult. The narrow approach road forced firefighters to park their vehicle some distance away.\nFirefighters from the Alandi municipal council and the Pimpri Chinchwad Municipal Corporation battled the blaze for over two hours before bringing it under control. Volunteers from Shivtej Mitra Mandal helped in the rescue and firefighting.\nA second fire broke out between 1am and 1.30am in a first-floor room of the pilgrims’ accommodation at Sant Jalaram Bappa temple on Alandi-Markal Road. No casualties were reported; some household articles were damaged.\nThe exact cause of both fires is yet to be established. Sandeep Patil, a junior engineer with Mahavitaran in Alandi, said the preliminary assessment pointed to a possible short circuit in the first fire, as the insulation on the electrical wires had burnt while the wires remained intact.","i":"illustration-df4a72b6d7","a":["Alandi","Alandi Devachi"]},{"u":"pune/hadapsar-bungalow-burglary-48-lakh-stolen-family-asleep-lakshmi-puja.html","h":"Hadapsar bungalow burglary: ₹48 lakh stolen while family was asleep after Lakshmi Puja","s":"Hadapsar Police have registered a burglary case against unidentified persons after thieves allegedly took gold jewellery and ₹12 lakh in cash from a bungalow.","k":"Hadapsar burglary","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-11T14:49:34+05:30","g":["Hadapsar","Burglary","Lakshmi Puja"],"b":"Unidentified thieves allegedly broke into a bungalow in Hadapsar at around 1:30 am on November 9 and escaped with gold jewellery and ₹12 lakh in cash.\nThe bungalow is at Netaji Subhash Gruharachana Society, opposite Annasaheb Magar College. The thieves allegedly got in by removing the glass from a window in the pooja room while the family was asleep after Lakshmi Puja celebrations.\nThe theft came to light the next morning. The total value of the stolen property is estimated at ₹48 lakh.\nA 49-year-old resident filed a complaint, and Hadapsar Police registered a burglary case against unidentified persons. Further investigation is under way.","i":"illustration-c32e21e89b","a":["Hadapsar"]},{"u":"pune/pune-fifth-most-congested-city-tomtom-traffic-index-2025.html","h":"Pune ranked world’s fifth most congested city; commuters lose over six days a year in traffic jams","s":"In Pune’s evening peak, a 10 km journey takes 41 minutes and 40 seconds, with vehicles moving at an average of just 14.4 kmph.","k":"Pune traffic","c":"City","t":"2026-11-11T14:33:59+05:30","g":["Pune traffic","Traffic congestion","Rush hour"],"b":"Pune ranked fifth among 492 cities worldwide in the TomTom Traffic Index 2025, and its commuters lose over six days a year in rush-hour traffic jams.\nThe city’s average congestion level in the index was 71.1%. Pune is India’s second most congested city, after Bengaluru, which ranked second in the world at 74.4%. Mumbai ranked 18th at 63.2%, and New Delhi 23rd.\nThe time Pune commuters lose comes to 152 hours, or six days and eight hours, a year, which is nearly nine hours more in 2025 than the year before. The average congestion level rose by 5.4 percentage points over 2024.\nA 10 km journey in Pune takes an average of 33 minutes and 20 seconds. The same distance takes about 38 minutes and 13 seconds in the morning rush hour, and 41 minutes and 40 seconds in the evening peak, when vehicles move at an average of just 14.4 kmph.","i":"illustration-fb06399f1c","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pune-dowry-case-police-recover-35-tolas-gold-hunt-remaining-15.html","h":"Pune dowry case: police recover 35 tolas of gold, hunt for remaining 15","s":"Police custody of a woman’s husband and in-laws was extended by two days in a case of alleged dowry harassment and abetment of her suicide, and the defence opposed the extension.","k":"Dowry case","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-11T14:08:26+05:30","g":["Dowry case","Swargate police station","Pune City Police"],"b":"Pune police have recovered 35 of the 50 tolas of gold allegedly linked to dowry demands, and the remaining 15 tolas are yet to be recovered. The case, registered at Swargate police station, Pune City Police, is one of alleged dowry harassment and abetment of a woman’s suicide.\nOn November 9, First Class Judicial Magistrate Nandita K Mutha extended the police custody of the woman’s husband, father-in-law and mother-in-law by two days, saying further interrogation was necessary to complete the investigation.\nThe prosecution sought the extension, citing the pending gold recovery, the phone seizure and the search for the absconding accused. The defence opposed it.\nPolice are still tracing the mother-in-law’s mobile phone, allegedly used to make the dowry demands, and the accused sister-in-law, who remains absconding.","i":"illustration-ae349be6af","a":["Swargate"]},{"u":"pune/pmpml-500-new-cng-buses-november-end-tata-motors-fix-defects.html","h":"PMPML to add 500 new CNG buses by November-end; Tata Motors told to fix defects","s":"PMPML officials who inspected the new Tata Motors-built CNG buses in Lucknow found issues with support structures near the front and rear doors and with welding joints, and water testing showed leaks above the BRT doors.","k":"PMPML buses","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-11T13:57:53+05:30","g":["PMPML","CNG buses","Tata Motors","Pimpri-Chinchwad"],"b":"Defects have been found in the 500 new CNG buses that Tata Motors is building, and the company has been told to fix them before delivery. Pune Mahanagar Parivahan Mahamandal Limited (PMPML) expects the buses to join its fleet by the end of November.\nOf the 500 buses, PMPML will own 400 and a contractor will operate 100.\nPMPML officials inspected the buses in Lucknow before their induction. The shortcomings they found include issues with the support structures near the front and rear doors, welding joints and gaps in parts of the tubes. Water testing showed leaks above the BRT doors and near the door glass panels.\nTata Motors has also been told to ensure that IP-based rear-view cameras, dashcams, destination boards and vehicle tracking systems are properly installed and working. Sensors will also be fitted on both main doors of each bus.\nPMPML Chief Engineer Narayan Karde said the inspection team had communicated the technical issues to Tata Motors and told the company to resolve them before handing over the buses.\nPMPML Chairman and Managing Director Mahesh Awhad said the 500 buses would strengthen passenger services and increase capacity for commuters.\nPMPML's fleet stands at 1,961 buses: 684 of its own and 1,277 operated by contractors. The new buses are expected to improve public transport across Pune and Pimpri-Chinchwad.","i":"illustration-d1939d1a0f","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pune-yerawada-group-allegedly-attacks-young-man-iron-knuckles-stones-cctv.html","h":"Yerawada: group allegedly attacks young man with iron knuckles, stones; CCTV emerges","s":"CCTV footage has emerged of a group allegedly attacking a young man in Laxminagar, Yerawada, and Yerawada Police have registered a case.","k":"Yerawada","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-11T13:22:02+05:30","g":["Pune","Yerawada","Laxminagar","CCTV"],"b":"A group allegedly attacked a young man with iron knuckles and stones in the Laxminagar area of Yerawada in the early hours of 9 November, leaving him seriously injured.\nCCTV footage of the incident has now emerged, and Yerawada Police have registered a case in connection with it.","i":"","a":["Yerawada","Yerwada","Yeravda","Yerawda","Yerwda"]},{"u":"pune/kolkata-airport-hijack-threat-alert-air-india-ai-772-passengers-taken-off.html","h":"Kolkata airport hijack threat alert on Mumbai-bound Air India flight AI 772; passengers taken off","s":"Authorities have not established whether a possible hijack threat on Air India flight AI 772 was genuine, and no actual hijacking or injury had been confirmed.","k":"Kolkata airport","c":"City","t":"2026-11-11T13:10:12+05:30","g":["Air India","AI 772","Kolkata airport","Hijack threat","Mumbai"],"b":"Air India flight AI 772, an Airbus A320neo bound for Mumbai, was the subject of a suspected hijack threat that came to light shortly before take-off on Wednesday morning, 11 November, at Kolkata’s Netaji Subhas Chandra Bose International Airport.\nThe pilot alerted Air Traffic Control (ATC) about a possible security concern when the aircraft was preparing to depart for Mumbai. The aircraft was then moved to an isolation bay for detailed security checks. Passengers were taken off the aircraft as security personnel began the required procedures.\nA message indicating a possible hijack threat is said to have been found inside the aircraft shortly before departure. It is said to have been written either on the mirror in the aircraft’s washroom or on a note or slip found on board.\nThe exact location and form of the message have not been independently confirmed. Authorities have not established who may have written it or whether the threat was genuine.\nThere was no confirmation of an actual hijacking, an attempt to take control of the aircraft or any injury to passengers or crew. The outcome of the security inspection and the flight arrangements that followed had not been confirmed, and further official information is awaited.","i":"illustration-f0e704e819","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pune-mhada-lottery-record-61-applicants-every-home.html","h":"MHADA Pune lottery: record 61 applicants for every home","s":"The MHADA Pune Board's lottery of 4,462 homes received 3,25,077 applications, and the draw is scheduled for December 1.","k":"MHADA lottery","c":"City","t":"2026-11-11T12:53:56+05:30","g":["MHADA","MHADA Pune Board","Housing lottery","EWS","LIG"],"b":"The Maharashtra Housing and Area Development Authority (MHADA) Pune Board's lottery of 4,462 homes has drawn a record response: an average of 61 applicants for each home, the highest the board has ever received for a housing lottery.\nApplications opened on August 24 and closed on October 30. A total of 3,25,077 applications were submitted, and 2,74,068 applicants paid the earnest money deposit needed to enter the draw. In earlier lotteries the board received a maximum of around 2.25 lakh applications with deposits.\nOfficials said the response was significantly higher than anticipated. According to officials, the Pune Board has collected about Rs 567.54 crore in deposits and fees.\nThe homes, under the 15% integrated housing scheme and the 20% comprehensive housing scheme, are in the economically weaker section (EWS) and low-income group (LIG) categories. The board extended the deadline three times over technical difficulties. Between October 16 and 20 the MahaIT system was unavailable, halting document verification.\nThe earnest money deposit is Rs 15,000 for EWS homes and Rs 20,000 for LIG homes, plus an application fee of Rs 708. The draw is scheduled for December 1. Deposits of unsuccessful applicants will be refunded after the draw; the Rs 708 fee is not refundable.\nThe applications will now be scrutinised and the final list of eligible applicants published.","i":"illustration-f8c98d59d0","a":[]},{"u":"pune/national-obc-mukti-morcha-demands-pune-renamed-phule-nagar.html","h":"National OBC Mukti Morcha demands Pune be renamed ‘Phule Nagar’","s":"National OBC Mukti Morcha, which wants Pune renamed ‘Phule Nagar’, also seeks the state government’s intervention in pursuing the Bharat Ratna for Mahatma Jyotiba Phule with the Centre, a special one-day session of the state legislature and a ‘Satyashodhak Bhushan’ award.","k":"Pune renaming","c":"Politics","t":"2026-11-11T12:43:18+05:30","g":["Pune","Phule Nagar","Jyotiba Phule","Bharat Ratna","Maharashtra"],"b":"A delegation of National OBC Mukti Morcha office-bearers recently met Chief Minister Devendra Fadnavis in Nagpur and submitted a memorandum demanding that Pune be renamed ‘Phule Nagar’ in honour of Mahatma Jyotiba Phule.\nThe organisation wants the renaming to mark Phule’s upcoming bicentenary. In the memorandum it urged the state government to pass an official resolution proposing the renaming and to initiate the necessary process.\nThe organisation said Phule made invaluable contributions to education and social reform. Since Pune was closely associated with his work and social reform movements, it said, renaming the city would be a tribute to his legacy.\nThe memorandum also sought the state government’s intervention in pursuing the Bharat Ratna for Phule with the Centre. In March 2025, the Maharashtra Legislative Assembly unanimously passed a resolution recommending the honour posthumously for both Jyotiba Phule and his wife, Savitribai Phule.\nAmong the organisation’s other demands are a special one-day session of the state legislature to discuss Phule’s contributions, and special general body meetings in local self-government institutions across Maharashtra on April 11, 2027, to mark his birth anniversary.\nThe delegation also proposed a ‘Satyashodhak Bhushan’ award for individuals and organisations working towards social awareness, progressive causes and development.","i":"","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pune-pmc-cancels-thursday-water-cut-regular-supply-continue.html","h":"Pune: PMC cancels Thursday’s water cut, regular supply to continue","s":"The PMC Water Supply Department has announced that the water cut scheduled for Thursday, 12 November will not take place and that no planned interruption is expected on Thursday.","k":"Pune water supply","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-11T12:27:46+05:30","g":["Pune","PMC","water cut","water supply"],"b":"The water cut scheduled for Thursday, 12 November, has been cancelled by PMC, and water supply across Pune will run on its regular schedule.\nThe scheduled water cut will not take place. No planned interruption is expected on Thursday. Water supply across the city will continue as per the regular schedule.\nThe PMC Water Supply Department issued the announcement.","i":"illustration-3dfb3f1a7e","a":[]},{"u":"pune/dhangekar-taunts-bjp-leader-chandrakant-patil-grandson-kirloskars.html","h":"Dhangekar taunts BJP leader Chandrakant Patil: “Were you some grandson of the Kirloskars?”","s":"Former MLA Ravindra Dhangekar warned that “Nobody’s power is permanent” and that power in one place today can go elsewhere tomorrow.","k":"Kolhapur politics","c":"Politics","t":"2026-11-11T12:17:04+05:30","g":["Ravindra Dhangekar","Chandrakant Patil","Satej Patil","Kolhapur"],"b":"Former MLA Ravindra Dhangekar taunts BJP leader Chandrakant Patil with the question “Were you some grandson of the Kirloskars?”, after Congress leader Satej Patil replied to Chandrakant Patil’s criticism over his wealth. Kolhapur politics has heated up over allegations traded between Congress leader Satej Patil and Chandrakant Patil. Dhangekar too hit out at Chandrakant Patil.\n“Satej Patil’s father D.Y. Patil used to ride a scooter, that is fine. But Maharashtra has seen your situation too. You used to stand outside hotels with a shabnam bag, waiting for someone to take you in and buy you tea. Were you some grandson of the Kirloskars?”\nDhangekar asked\nDhangekar said he had heard Chandrakant Patil’s speech and that what is going on now looks like a quarrel at a water tap. He alleged that intimidation was being done with “I will do this, I will do that” language.\n“Nobody’s power is permanent,” he warned. He added that power in one place today can go elsewhere tomorrow and those in power should remember it.\nChandrakant Patil had asked how Satej Patil’s property grew so much when his father D.Y. Patil once rode a scooter. He had alleged that Satej Patil wants control of the Gokul milk union “to eat the cream”.\nSatej Patil replied that Chandrakant Patil too now has a glass bungalow. He told him not to issue threats from within the government machinery, and challenged him to fight each other in the Assembly election.","i":"","a":[]},{"u":"pune/baburao-sanas-ground-pmc-proposes-pass-system-for-athletes.html","h":"Baburao Sanas Ground: PMC proposes pass system for athletes at ₹300 to ₹600 a month","s":"Individual athletes now use Pune's Late Baburao Sanas Ground free of cost, and a PMC proposal for a new pass system takes effect only after General Body approval.","k":"Baburao Sanas Ground","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-11T12:06:31+05:30","g":["Baburao Sanas Ground","PMC","Pune Municipal Corporation","Sports Department"],"b":"Athletes who practise individually at Pune's Late Baburao Sanas Ground may soon pay ₹300 a month if they are below 18 and ₹600 if they are above 18, under a Pune Municipal Corporation (PMC) proposal for a new pass system.\nIndividual athletes use the ground free of cost at present.\nUnder the proposed policy, practice will be allowed between 6 am and 9 am and between 4 pm and 7 pm. 9 am to 4 pm will be reserved for competitions, and regular practice will not be permitted while competitions are underway.\nThe ground will stay closed every Sunday for maintenance and will not be available for walking.\nAthletes must wear proper sports shoes on the synthetic track and ground. Slippers and regular shoes will not be allowed, and food is banned on the track and ground. Parents of trainees and other citizens will not be allowed inside.\nAthletes and coaches will need identity cards from the Sports Department. The policy says athletes and coaches will be responsible for any injuries or accidents during practice, and the civic administration will not be held liable.\nThe proposal has been placed before the PMC Standing Committee and General Body through the civic body's Sports Committee, and will come into effect only after approval from the General Body.","i":"illustration-120f5eb1f8","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pune-fda-destroys-93-kg-sweets-suspends-licences-wanowrie-units.html","h":"Pune FDA destroys 93 kg of sweets, suspends licences of two Wanowrie units","s":"Following alleged food safety violations, two Wanowrie sweet manufacturing units, MA Karachi Sweets Mart and Shri Mohan Karachi Sweets Mart, were ordered to have their licences suspended with immediate effect.","k":"Wanowrie","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-11T11:55:47+05:30","g":["Pune","FDA","Food safety","Wanowrie"],"b":"Two sweet manufacturing units in Wanowrie were raided by the Pune Food and Drug Administration (FDA) on 10 November 2026. Officials seized and destroyed 93 kg of suspected substandard or unsafe sweets.\nThe units are MA Karachi Sweets Mart and Shri Mohan Karachi Sweets Mart. The raid was carried out under the Safe Food, Safe Maharashtra campaign.\nThe sweets, including motichoor laddus, boondi and barfi, were worth ₹50,860.\nFollowing the alleged food safety violations, the licences of both units were ordered to be suspended with immediate effect. Samples have been sent to a laboratory for further testing.\nThe FDA has warned of strict action against establishments that violate food safety standards.","i":"","a":["Wanowrie","Wanawadi","Wanwadi","Wanowri","Wanavdi"]},{"u":"pune/pune-woman-raises-data-privacy-concerns-after-rapido-rider-whatsapp-message.html","h":"Pune woman raises data privacy concerns after Rapido rider's WhatsApp message","s":"A woman in Pune who complained to Rapido has questioned the need to share actual phone numbers, citing the possibility of misuse.","k":"Rapido data privacy","c":"City","t":"2026-11-11T11:32:31+05:30","g":["Pune","Rapido","Data privacy"],"b":"A 21-year-old woman in Pune, who says she took a Rapido bike taxi from Swargate Metro Station to Kondhwa, has raised data privacy concerns after allegedly receiving a personal WhatsApp message from the rider following the ride.\nAccording to the woman, during the journey the rider repeatedly stared at her and allegedly drove at high speed, making her uncomfortable. She further alleged that he followed her after the journey and contacted her on WhatsApp shortly after the ride ended.\nShe has questioned how the rider got her personal number and why riders can access passengers' private information. Rapido's privacy policy says customers' names, pickup addresses and contact details are shared with its Captains (riders) to help them locate and contact passengers.\nShe suggested that calls and messages go through a secure, privacy-protected system within the app, and questioned the need to share actual phone numbers, citing the possibility of misuse.\nThe woman lodged a complaint with Rapido, and its support team told her it had suspended the Captain's account.","i":"illustration-0954e64c9f","a":[]},{"u":"pune/major-fire-old-wada-opposite-church-guruwar-peth.html","h":"Major fire at old wada opposite church in Guruwar Peth","s":"Residents are concerned, the cause is not yet known and there is no official word yet on casualties or damage.","k":"Guruwar Peth","c":"Accidents and fires","t":"2026-11-11T10:48:49+05:30","g":["Guruwar Peth","Pune Fire Brigade","Fire"],"b":"A major fire broke out at an old wada opposite a church in the Guruwar Peth area of Pune, and fire tenders from the Pune Fire Brigade were sent to the spot to bring the flames under control.\nThe wada is a traditional residential building, and the fire caused concern among residents.\nThe cause of the fire is not yet known. There is no official word yet on casualties, injuries or the extent of damage to property. Further details are awaited.","i":"","a":["Guruwar Peth","Guruvar Peth","Guruwar Pet"]},{"u":"pune/pune-residents-allegedly-cheated-digital-arrest-fake-challans-crypto-scams.html","h":"Pune residents allegedly cheated of lakhs in digital arrest threats, fake challans and crypto investment scams","s":"A 75-year-old woman from Karvenagar, an Ambegaon Budruk resident, a young businessman and a businessman living in a society along Pune-Satara Road were allegedly cheated of ₹32 lakh, ₹5.20 lakh, ₹5.13 lakh and ₹6.81 lakh.","k":"Digital arrest","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-10T22:12:27+05:30","g":["Digital arrest","Fake challans","Crypto investment scams","Karvenagar","Warje Police"],"b":"Pune residents were allegedly cheated of lakhs in digital arrest threats, fake challans and crypto investment scams, among them a 75-year-old woman from Karvenagar who was allegedly cheated of ₹32 lakh.\nOn November 6, callers told her that a case had been registered against her over an alleged ₹2 crore financial fraud involving a bank in Nashik. They threatened her with a so-called digital arrest and warned that her property would be seized.\nShe transferred ₹32 lakh through RTGS transactions over two to three days. She realised she had been cheated when they demanded more.\nWarje Police registered a case in the Karvenagar fraud. Police Inspector Suvarna Hulwan of the Crime Branch is investigating.\nAn Ambegaon Budruk resident was allegedly cheated of ₹5.20 lakh by fraudsters posing as officials from the Department of Telecommunications in Delhi. They claimed his mobile number had been used for drug trafficking and threatened him with arrest.\nAfter fraudsters lured him with promises of lucrative returns through cryptocurrency investments, a young businessman was allegedly cheated of ₹5.13 lakh.\nA businessman living in a society along Pune-Satara Road was allegedly cheated of ₹6.81 lakh. Fraudsters sent him a fake traffic challan and threatened legal action, and allegedly misused his bank account details to withdraw money.\nBharati Vidyapeeth, Bibwewadi and Swargate police stations received complaints. Those cases are being investigated by Police Inspector Rangrao Pawar of the Crime Branch, Senior Police Inspector Ashwini Satpute and Police Inspector Vikas Bharmal of the Crime Branch.","i":"illustration-dd8694d2ae","a":["Karvenagar"]},{"u":"pune/car-allegedly-wrong-side-rams-two-wheeler-shinde-bridge-shivane.html","h":"Shinde Bridge, Shivane: car allegedly on wrong side rams two-wheeler, driver detained","s":"Angry locals confronted the driver at the spot before police personnel took him into custody; the rider's condition is awaited.","k":"Shivane","c":"Accidents and fires","t":"2026-11-10T21:59:54+05:30","g":["Pune","Shivane","Shinde Bridge","Warje"],"b":"On Monday night, a car allegedly driven on the wrong side of the road and at high speed rammed a two-wheeler on Shinde Bridge in Shivane, near the Warje-Kothrud belt.\nLocal residents and eyewitnesses allege the driver was intoxicated.\nAngry locals gathered at the spot and confronted the driver, and some residents allegedly assaulted him before police personnel reached the scene and took him into custody.\nShinde Bridge is a key connecting route in the Shivane area near Warje and Kothrud. Details of the two-wheeler rider's condition and the action taken against the driver are awaited.","i":"","a":["Shivane","Shivne","Warje","Warje Malwadi"]},{"u":"pune/two-groups-allegedly-clash-bhekrainagar-street-fight-video-viral.html","h":"Bhekrainagar erupts in violent street fight as two groups allegedly clash, video goes viral","s":"Concerns over public safety and law and order have been raised.","k":"Bhekrainagar","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-10T21:46:32+05:30","g":["Pune","Bhekrainagar","Street fight","Law and order"],"b":"Two groups allegedly got into a violent street fight in Bhekrainagar, Pune, and a video of it has gone viral on social media.\nThe video shows men kicking and assaulting each other. It has raised concerns over public safety and law and order.","i":"","a":["Bhekrainagar"]},{"u":"pune/tinhewadi-khed-three-minors-allegedly-attack-youth-koyta-vehicle-cut-row.html","h":"Tinhewadi, Khed: three minors allegedly launch life-threatening koyta attack on youth over old vehicle-cut row","s":"A 26-year-old seriously injured with a koyta has been admitted to hospital, and In-charge Police Inspector Santosh Girigosavi said police detained all three from Rakshewadi.","k":"Khed","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-10T21:19:50+05:30","g":["Pune","Khed","Tinhewadi","Koyta attack"],"b":"Three minors allegedly launched a life-threatening koyta attack on a 26-year-old on the road in Tinhewadi, Khed, on Tuesday, 10 November, at about 2:45 pm, while he was riding a two-wheeler.\nThe three allegedly struck his head and hands in the sudden attack. He was seriously injured and has been admitted to hospital for treatment. Worse was averted when local residents and passers-by raised an alarm.\nThe three are said to have held a grudge over a minor argument, caused a few days earlier by a vehicle being cut off.\nThe attack, in the middle of the road during the Diwali Padwa festivities, has caused a stir in Tinhewadi and the surrounding area, and residents are fearful.\nThe complaint was filed by the youth’s cousin. In-charge Police Inspector Santosh Girigosavi said police reached the spot, traced the attackers and detained all three from Rakshewadi.","i":"illustration-e67ef2c730","a":["Khed","Khed taluka","Khed Pune","Tinhewadi"]},{"u":"pune/hinjawadi-society-dispute-turns-violent-48-year-old-man-shoulder-dislocated.html","h":"Hinjawadi society dispute turns violent, 48-year-old man’s shoulder dislocated","s":"Hinjawadi Police are investigating a registered case, and the 48-year-old man has a dislocated shoulder.","k":"Hinjawadi","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-10T19:32:38+05:30","g":["Hinjawadi","Blue Ridge Society","Hinjawadi Police","Society dispute"],"b":"A 48-year-old man at Hinjawadi’s Blue Ridge Society was left with a dislocated shoulder after the accused allegedly assaulted him over a previous complaint.\nThe residents’ dispute turned violent, and the accused also allegedly threatened his wife and children.\nHinjawadi Police have registered a case and are investigating.","i":"illustration-3ef770d647","a":["Hinjawadi","Hinjewadi","Hinjwadi","Hinjawadi Phase 1","Hinjawadi Phase 2","Hinjawadi Phase 3","Hinjewadi Phase 1","Hinjewadi Phase 2","Hinjewadi Phase 3"]},{"u":"pune/container-trailer-overturns-kamshet-old-mumbai-pune-highway.html","h":"Container trailer overturns at Kamshet on Old Mumbai-Pune Highway, traffic at a standstill","s":"The driver was injured, and commuters should expect delays on this route.","k":"Kamshet","c":"Accidents and fires","t":"2026-11-10T18:50:57+05:30","g":["Pune","Kamshet","Old Mumbai-Pune Highway","Container trailer"],"b":"Traffic came to a standstill on both sides of the Old Mumbai-Pune Highway at Kamshet after a container trailer travelling from Pune towards Mumbai overturned.\nThe driver lost control within the jurisdiction of Kamshet police station, and the trailer crossed into the opposite lane and overturned. Long queues of vehicles formed on both sides of the highway.\nThe driver was injured and rushed to a hospital for treatment. Highway police reached the spot, and work is under way to clear the road and restore traffic. Commuters on this route should expect delays.","i":"","a":["Kamshet"]},{"u":"pune/bhor-truck-drags-two-wheeler-300-metres-both-catch-fire-youth-dies.html","h":"In Bhor, truck drags two-wheeler for nearly 300 metres; both catch fire, youth dies","s":"Both vehicles were completely gutted, and the driver is said to have fled.","k":"Bhor, Rambaug Road","c":"Accidents and fires","t":"2026-11-10T18:36:49+05:30","g":["Bhor","Pune district","Road accident","Truck accident"],"b":"A speeding truck rammed into a two-wheeler on Rambaug Road in Bhor, Pune district, on Tuesday and dragged it for about 300 metres; both vehicles caught fire, and a young man died while another was seriously injured.\nPreliminary information is that the accident took place near Navlai Temple, in front of the Bhor Sub-District Hospital.\nInstead of stopping, the truck driver kept driving with the two-wheeler trapped underneath.\nThe friction from the dragging is said to have set off a fire that engulfed both vehicles, and the truck and the two-wheeler were completely gutted.\nOne of the riders died on the spot; the other suffered serious injuries. The truck driver is said to have abandoned the truck and fled. Further details are awaited.","i":"","a":["Bhor","Bhor taluka"]},{"u":"pune/bhor-youth-dead-another-seriously-injured-truck-drags-two-wheeler.html","h":"Bhor: youth dead, another seriously injured as truck drags two-wheeler 300 metres","s":"Both vehicles caught fire and were completely gutted.","k":"Bhor","c":"Accidents and fires","t":"2026-11-10T17:59:27+05:30","g":["Pune","Bhor","Rambaug Road","Pune district"],"b":"On Tuesday, 10 November, a speeding truck rammed a two-wheeler on Rambaug Road in Bhor, Pune district, and dragged it about 300 metres. One of the riders, a youth, died on the spot, while the other sustained serious injuries.\nThe accident occurred near Navlai Temple, in front of the Bhor Sub-District Hospital. Instead of stopping, the truck driver kept driving with the two-wheeler trapped underneath.\nThe friction is said to have triggered a fire, and the truck and the two-wheeler were completely gutted.\nThe truck driver is said to have abandoned the vehicle and fled from the scene. Further details are awaited.","i":"","a":["Bhor","Bhor taluka"]},{"u":"pune/janwadi-man-found-dead-wife-sister-in-law-booked-allegedly-abetting-suicide.html","h":"Janwadi man found dead; wife, sister-in-law booked for allegedly abetting suicide","s":"According to his mother's complaint, the unemployed man with outstanding debts was allegedly subjected to mental harassment by his wife and sister-in-law, and Assistant Police Inspector Snehal Patil is investigating.","k":"Janwadi","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-10T17:45:12+05:30","g":["Pune","Janwadi","Chaturshringi Police","Suicide"],"b":"Chaturshringi Police have booked the wife and sister-in-law of a 30-year-old man, who was found dead at his residence in Panch Pandav Society, Janwadi, on November 4, on charges of allegedly abetting his suicide.\nPolice said he died by suicide. His mother filed the complaint on which Chaturshringi Police registered a case against his wife (25) and sister-in-law (30).\nAccording to the complaint, he was unemployed and had outstanding debts. The two women allegedly argued with him frequently and subjected him to mental harassment over various issues.\nAssistant Police Inspector Snehal Patil is conducting further investigation.","i":"illustration-5bc893cbd8","a":["Janwadi","Janawadi"]},{"u":"pune/pune-cantonment-board-seeks-defence-ministry-nod-monetise-properties.html","h":"Pune Cantonment Board seeks Defence Ministry nod to monetise three properties","s":"The Pune Cantonment Board's monthly revenue is under ₹2 crore against a need of nearly ₹12 crore.","k":"Pune Cantonment Board","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-10T17:02:46+05:30","g":["Pune","Pune Cantonment Board","Koregaon Park","MG Road"],"b":"The Pune Cantonment Board has asked the Ministry of Defence for statutory approval to develop three prime properties in Koregaon Park, Dhobighat and MG Road for commercial use under the Public-Private Partnership (PPP) model, as it tries to tackle its growing financial crisis.\nThe properties are 5.43 acres of unused land in Koregaon Park, 1.5 acres in Dhobighat, and around 8,000–10,000 sq. ft. on MG Road, including an old court property.\nThe board needs nearly ₹12 crore every month for salary, pension and essential expenses, but its monthly revenue is less than ₹2 crore. It currently depends on grants from the Ministry of Defence to manage routine expenses, and received ₹25 crore in financial assistance from the ministry a few months ago.\nThe financial crunch has also affected basic civic services, with residents regularly raising complaints about civic issues.\nFurther action will be taken only after the ministry grants permission. According to the Executive Engineer, the proposal is awaiting the ministry’s approval.","i":"illustration-2f454637e5","a":["Koregaon Park","KP","Koregaon Park Annexe"]},{"u":"pune/nana-peth-woman-hit-on-head-with-sickle-firecracker-row.html","h":"Nana Peth: woman hit on head with sickle saving father in firecracker row, two arrested","s":"A counter-complaint by one of those held has also led to a separate case against the woman's father and two others.","k":"Nana Peth","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-10T16:12:25+05:30","g":["Pune","Nana Peth","Samarth police","Firecracker dispute"],"b":"Around 1.30 am on 9 November, a 21-year-old woman was struck on the head with a sickle near Hope Hospital at Patra Chawl in Nana Peth while trying to save her father in a firecracker dispute.\nShe collapsed on the spot after being struck and is undergoing treatment at Sassoon General Hospital.\nAccording to police, the dispute began on the night of 8 November, when one of the wheels of her father's rickshaw accidentally ran over a firecracker. Around 1.30 am, a group allegedly abused him and assaulted him with kicks and punches near Hope Hospital.\nPolice say that when the family intervened, one of the assailants allegedly tried to strike him on the head with a sickle; his daughter stepped in and was struck instead. The assailants fled.\nSamarth police have arrested two men, aged 26 and 18, both residents of Tadiwala Road. They have registered a case of attempt to murder against a 30-year-old Patra Chawl resident and his associates.\nA counter-complaint by one of the arrested men alleges that he and the other man were assaulted with an iron weapon in the same dispute. Police have registered a separate case on it against the woman's father and two others.","i":"illustration-4d1b7fb23d","a":["Nana Peth","Nana Pet"]},{"u":"pune/mahatma-phule-memorial-expansion-300-crore-land-acquisition-begin.html","h":"Mahatma Phule memorial expansion gets ₹300 crore; land acquisition to begin","s":"A total of 5,608 sq m will be acquired, and 592 owners and 326 tenants are to be rehabilitated.","k":"Phule memorial","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-10T15:42:36+05:30","g":["Mahatma Phule memorial","Pune Municipal Corporation","Land acquisition","Rehabilitation"],"b":"The state government has sanctioned ₹300 crore for the expansion of the Mahatma Jyotirao Phule memorial in Pune, and the Pune Municipal Corporation is ready to begin land acquisition and rehabilitation as soon as the code of conduct ends.\nA total of 5,608 sq m will be acquired under the MRTP Act: 5,310 sq m of private land and 298 sq m of road. 592 owners and 326 tenants across 101 CTS numbers are to be rehabilitated. The corporation's general body approved the rehabilitation proposal on 25 August.\nOwners will be offered compensation at four times the ready reckoner rate, or available flats of that value. Old tenants can take an available flat on rent or ₹15 lakh in cash.\nAvinash Sapkal, Deputy Commissioner, PMC, said the survey of all concerned is complete, clear rehabilitation options have been given to owners and tenants, and with the government's funds the focus will be on completing land acquisition quickly.\nThe Pune Municipal Corporation has completed the survey of the land and the property holders' details needed for the project. Of the sanctioned funds, ₹100 crore has reached the corporation, and the process for the rest is under way. The project, stalled for many years, is now expected to gather pace.","i":"illustration-64f717f2d8","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pmc-standing-committee-cleared-168-crore-road-upgrade-pune-grand-cycle-tour.html","h":"PMC standing committee clears ₹168 crore road upgrade for 2027 Pune Grand Cycle Tour route","s":"The upgrade covers 136 km within Pune city, for the six-day tour scheduled for January 26 to 31, 2027.","k":"Pune Grand Cycle Tour","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-10T15:30:00+05:30","g":["PMC","Pune Grand Cycle Tour","Road upgrade","Cycling"],"b":"The Pune Municipal Corporation’s standing committee has cleared tenders worth ₹168 crore, inclusive of GST, for a road upgrade covering 136 km of the 2027 Pune Grand Cycle Tour route within Pune city.\nThe six-day Pune Grand Cycle Tour is scheduled for January 26 to 31, 2027. While 52 km was developed for the first edition last year, another 84 km will now be taken up.\nContractors will level the stretches to a uniform surface suitable for competitive cycling. Damaged stretches and potholes will be repaired, dividers repainted, and fresh thermoplastic markings and signboards installed. Speed breakers and plastic barriers along the route are set to be removed. The upgraded roads will follow international standards and carry a 10-year defect liability period.\nFour contractors have been assigned through separate tender packages. An independent consultant has been appointed to oversee the work and monitor its quality.\nThe race will cross areas under the PMC, the Pimpri-Chinchwad Municipal Corporation and the PMRDA, besides other parts of the district, with cyclists from India and abroad expected to take part. PMC standing committee chairman Shrinath Bhimale said the approved allocation would cover the required improvements across the route.\nThe entire course will undergo inspection and trial runs before the competition.","i":"illustration-2fadfb0bce","a":[]},{"u":"pune/loni-kalbhor-ex-sarpanch-kalbhor-four-booked-allegedly-assaulting-hotel-owner.html","h":"Loni Kalbhor: ex-sarpanch Rahul Kalbhor among four booked for allegedly assaulting hotel owner, staff","s":"The dispute began over a food bill paid online, the hotel owner's complaint says, and Loni Kalbhor Police are investigating.","k":"Loni Kalbhor","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-10T15:17:09+05:30","g":["Pune","Loni Kalbhor","Rahul Kalbhor","Jagdamba Hotel"],"b":"Rahul Kalbhor, a former Loni Kalbhor sarpanch, is among four booked for allegedly assaulting a hotel owner, staff and a customer at Jagdamba Hotel in Kadamwakvasti on Monday night, 9 November.\nThe hotel is near Angel High School in Loni Kalbhor. A minor dispute over a food bill allegedly escalated into several assaults there.\nAccording to the hotel owner's complaint, it began after the former sarpanch's brother paid his food bill online and asked whether the payment had been received. A dispute allegedly followed, during which he abused and assaulted the owner's son.\nRahul Kalbhor and the other accused allegedly returned to the hotel with others and assaulted the owner, staff members and a customer who had stepped in to calm the situation.\nThe complaint further states that when the owner's son and his cousin were returning from the police station after reporting the incident, the four accused allegedly stopped and assaulted them near a pizza outlet.\nAll four accused are residents of Loni Kalbhor. Loni Kalbhor Police have registered a case under relevant sections of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita (BNS), and further investigation is underway.","i":"illustration-a5eaa01093","a":["Loni Kalbhor"]},{"u":"pune/pune-suicide-case-husband-in-laws-custody-extended-gold-seized.html","h":"Pune suicide case: husband, in-laws’ custody extended; 35 tolas of gold seized","s":"15 of the 50 tolas of gold are yet to be recovered.","k":"Pune suicide case","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-10T15:03:54+05:30","g":["Pune","Suicide case","Custody","Gold"],"b":"The husband, mother-in-law and father-in-law of a woman have had their custody extended in a Pune suicide case.\nOf 50 tolas of gold, 35 have been seized, and the remaining 15 tolas are yet to be recovered.","i":"illustration-d4b2a085f0","a":[]},{"u":"pune/sahakarnagar-inspector-alleges-two-officers-confined-him-nearly-three-hours.html","h":"Sahakarnagar inspector alleges two officers confined him for nearly three hours","s":"A Sahakarnagar police inspector alleges that two fellow officers confined him in his office and threatened to implicate him in a false molestation case, an incident he claims was captured entirely on CCTV cameras installed inside the police station.","k":"Sahakarnagar Police Station","c":"City","t":"2026-11-10T14:50:55+05:30","g":["Sahakarnagar","Sahakarnagar Police Station","Police inspector"],"b":"Police Inspector Rajesh Dnyanoba Khandve of Sahakarnagar Police Station alleges that two fellow officers, Assistant Police Inspector Sonali Mithare and Senior Police Inspector Vitthal Pawar, confined him inside his own office for nearly three hours, threatened to implicate him in a false molestation case and deliberately humiliated him; according to his statement, the incident occurred late on November 6.\nAs he was due to go on leave the next day, he returned to the police station between 11 pm and midnight to collect a bundle of books and other personal belongings from his office, according to his statement.\nIn a written statement submitted on November 7, Khandve alleged that the two officers acted in connivance to intimidate, verbally abuse and defame him. He claimed the entire incident was captured on CCTV cameras installed inside the police station.\nKhandve alleged that while he was sitting in the crime branch office, Mithare entered, questioned why he was at the police station at such a late hour and why he frequently visited at odd hours, threatened to register a molestation case against him and used abusive language despite his repeated explanation that he had come only to collect his belongings.","i":"illustration-bc6321dccb","a":["Sahakarnagar"]},{"u":"pune/pune-nashik-highway-chakan-two-bikers-stop-st-bus-beat-driver.html","h":"Two bikers stop ST bus at Chakan on Pune–Nashik highway, brutally beat driver","s":"Passengers on an ST bus at Chakan repeatedly pleaded with two young men who assaulted its driver, but the beating did not stop.","k":"Chakan","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-10T14:38:11+05:30","g":["Chakan","ST bus","Pune–Nashik highway","ST drivers"],"b":"Two bikers stopped an ST bus on the Pune–Nashik highway at Chakan by putting their two-wheeler across its path, and brutally beat the driver.\nThe bus was travelling from Pune towards Nashik. Passengers on board repeatedly pleaded with the two young men, but the two did not stop the beating.\nThe attack, in the middle of the highway, left passengers frightened and has again raised the question of ST drivers’ safety.","i":"","a":["Chakan"]},{"u":"pune/dhayari-shivajinagar-pmpml-bus-ticketless-passenger-fined-500-heated-argument.html","h":"Dhayari–Shivajinagar PMPML bus: ticketless passenger or careless conductor? High drama, ₹500 fine","s":"The commuter, fined ₹500, says the conductor was busy talking to the driver when he asked for a ticket, and fellow passengers back his account.","k":"PMPML bus 17","c":"City","t":"2026-11-10T14:24:56+05:30","g":["PMPML","Dhayari","Shivajinagar","Bus ticket"],"b":"A three-member inspection squad found a commuter without a valid ticket on PMPML bus number 17 on the Dhayari–Shivajinagar route, leading to high drama and a heated argument near the NuMaVi bus stop in Appa Balwant Chowk on Tuesday morning, around 10:30 am.\nThe commuter, who had boarded at Swargate, said he had repeatedly called for a ticket but the conductor was busy talking to the driver. The conductor claimed the passenger did not respond when asked.\nThe passenger refused to get off and offered to buy a ticket on the spot. The checkers boarded the moving bus and fined him ₹500 before getting off near Dakshinmukhi Maruti.\nFellow passengers backed the commuter's account, alleging that the conductor had ignored calls for a ticket while chatting near the driver's cabin.","i":"","a":["Dhayari","Dhayri","Dhayarigaon","Shivajinagar","Shivajinagar Gaothan"]},{"u":"pune/pune-senior-citizen-approaches-police-model-colony-flat-listed-online.html","h":"Pune senior citizen approaches police against unauthorised online listing of Model Colony flat for Rs 5 crore","s":"An advertisement for a retired Pune senior citizen’s flat, posted on an online property platform in the name of a real estate agency, was removed by an agent who posted it after his complaint to police.","k":"Model Colony flat listing","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-10T14:12:01+05:30","g":["Pune","Model Colony","Senior citizens","Chaturshringi police"],"b":"A retired senior citizen in Pune has gone to the cybercrime cell and Chaturshringi police after his four-BHK flat in Model Colony was advertised online for Rs 5 crore, though he had no plans to sell it and had authorised no one to advertise it.\n“Who put my flat up for sale?”\nThe advertisement offered the 2,758 sq ft flat, on the 12th floor of Dharmesh Apartment near Dhotre Chowk, and was posted on an online property platform in the name of a real estate agency.\nIn his complaint, he said he had neither put the flat on the market nor authorised any property dealer to advertise it. He fears someone could be attempting a property transaction without his consent. He sought a probe and submitted a copy of the advertisement.\nThe agent who posted the listing removed it after the complaint. Police are now trying to establish who approached the agent and instructed him to advertise the flat, and are probing the motive.\nPolice have appealed to senior citizens facing harassment to approach their local police station or lodge a complaint directly at the police commissioner’s office, and to report any attempt to conduct property transactions without their consent.","i":"illustration-cce8c07d70","a":["Model Colony"]},{"u":"pune/akurdi-pcmc-water-pipeline-bursts-near-chintamani-temple-lakhs-litres-wasted.html","h":"Akurdi: PCMC drinking water pipeline bursts near Chintamani Temple, lakhs of litres wasted","s":"Residents and local shopkeepers want accountability and routine maintenance audits of underground utilities, saying water was allowed to drain away for hours.","k":"Akurdi water pipeline","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-10T13:58:08+05:30","g":["Akurdi","PCMC","Water supply","Chintamani Temple"],"b":"A major drinking water pipeline of the Pimpri-Chinchwad Municipal Corporation (PCMC) burst near Chintamani Temple in Akurdi, wasting lakhs of litres and sending clean water onto nearby streets.\nThe road stretch turned into a waterlogged stream, disrupting pedestrian and vehicular movement.\nResidents and local shopkeepers voiced anger over what they called the civic administration's delayed emergency response. They said drinking water was allowed to drain away for hours despite regular water cuts and shortages in neighbouring areas.\nThey have demanded accountability and routine maintenance audits of underground utilities. They urged the PCMC water supply department to contain the leak and restore the pipeline immediately.","i":"","a":["Akurdi"]},{"u":"pune/warje-drunk-wrong-side-driver-hits-two-wheeler-residents-assault-him.html","h":"Warje: drunk wrong-side driver hits two-wheeler on Shivane–Shinde bridge, residents assault him","s":"The rider was injured, and personnel from the local police station took the accused driver into custody.","k":"Warje bridge crash","c":"Accidents and fires","t":"2026-11-10T13:44:25+05:30","g":["Warje","Warje Malwadi","Shivane–Shinde bridge","Wrong-side driver"],"b":"On the Shivane–Shinde bridge in Warje Malwadi, local residents assaulted an intoxicated car driver after he collided head-on with a two-wheeler while speeding in the wrong direction.\nThe two-wheeler was severely damaged and its rider injured.\nAgitated local residents gathered at the spot after the crash, stopped the driver, smashed the car's windows and assaulted him before police intervened.\nPersonnel from the local police station rushed to the scene and brought the situation under control. They took the accused into custody and shifted the injured to a nearby hospital for treatment.","i":"","a":["Warje","Warje Malwadi"]},{"u":"pune/yerawada-over-200-jadhavnagar-residents-protest-sra-survey-halted.html","h":"‘Unacceptable’: Yerawada scheme protest by over 200 Jadhavnagar residents, survey halted","s":"Residents are demanding criminal action against developer Lalit Sakhare and Pashchim Builders and the restoration of the earlier 70% threshold; Sakhare has refuted the charges, calling them fabricated.","k":"Yerawada SRA scheme","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-10T12:48:26+05:30","g":["Yerawada","Jadhavnagar","SRA","Slum Rehabilitation"],"b":"SRA Secretary Sheetal Nikam announced the immediate suspension of the ongoing survey of the Jadhavnagar redevelopment scheme in Yerawada after more than 200 residents marched to the Slum Rehabilitation Authority (SRA) office.\nThe proposed SRA project in Yerawada has triggered major unrest. Protesting under the banner of the Jadhavnagar SRA Virodhi Kruti Samiti, residents demanded criminal action against developer Lalit Sakhare and Pashchim Builders.\nThey accuse the developer of relying on forged documents, bogus names and manipulated consent papers to push the redevelopment scheme through.\nThe residents also demanded that the 51% consent rule be scrapped and the earlier 70% threshold restored, to prevent misuse by builders. They have warned that the protest will intensify.\nNikam met the protesters and assured a joint hearing with the SRA Chief Executive Officer next week to probe the allegations.\nLalit Sakhare has refuted the charges, calling the allegations fabricated.","i":"illustration-e940b19427","a":["Yerawada","Yerwada","Yeravda","Yerawda","Yerwda"]},{"u":"pune/pcmc-hawker-zone-plan-stalls-only-1506-of-15013-vendors-have-certificates.html","h":"PCMC hawker zone plan stalls: only 1,506 of 15,013 eligible street vendors have certificates","s":"Without official documentation, thousands of street vendors are vulnerable to action by the encroachment department, and the Supreme Court has questioned the delay.","k":"PCMC hawker zones","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-10T12:35:34+05:30","g":["PCMC","Hawker zones","Street vendors","Supreme Court"],"b":"The Pimpri-Chinchwad Municipal Corporation (PCMC) has identified 41 hawker zones across the city, but only 1,506 of 15,013 eligible street vendors have registration certificates so far.\nYears after the survey was conducted, issuing certificates and developing designated vending areas remains incomplete.\nThe delay has left thousands of street vendors without official documentation, making them vulnerable to action by the encroachment department. Some vendors are said to have had their goods seized and suffered financial losses.\nFollowing complaints and legal proceedings, the Supreme Court has questioned the delay and directed the civic administration to speed up the distribution of certificates and the identification of vending zones.\nThe PCMC has begun distributing certificates. The remaining eligible vendors are still waiting for recognition and designated spaces to do business.","i":"illustration-f89f5cd51d","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pune-revised-draft-development-plan-narrowing-50-roads-undri-highway.html","h":"Major changes: Pune revised draft Development Plan proposes narrowing 50 roads and Undri highway","s":"Under the revised plan, which is now awaiting final approval, four 36-metre roads would become 24 metres wide and the state highway through Undri 45 metres.","k":"Development Plan","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-10T12:22:41+05:30","g":["Pune","Development Plan","Undri","Roads"],"b":"Major changes in Pune's revised draft Development Plan: roads originally planned at 36 metres have been reduced to as little as 24 metres. The plan proposes narrowing 50 roads in eight merged village areas and the Undri highway.\nThe proposed width of the state highway passing through Undri has been reduced from 60 metres to 45 metres. Several 12-metre roads have been narrowed to nine metres.\nThe affected areas are Lohegaon (12 roads), Mundhwa (Keshav Nagar, 7), Hadapsar (Sadesatranali, 5), Undri (6), Ambegaon Budruk (4), Ambegaon Khurd (1), Dhayari (6) and Shivane-Uttamnagar (9).\nThe breakdown: four 36-metre roads reduced to 24 metres; two 30-metre roads to 24 or 15 metres; 20 roads of 24 metres to 18, 15 or 12 metres; 15 roads of 18 metres to 15 or 12 metres; four 15-metre roads to 12 metres; and five 12-metre roads to nine metres.\nThe authorities have cited provisions in the regional development plan, existing structures, approved layouts, land acquisition status, natural drainage channels and canal boundaries. Land released from the road alignments will be added to adjoining residential zones, reserved plots or other land-use categories.\nThe changes have raised concerns about long-term connectivity and traffic movement in these fast-growing areas, where unauthorised construction has already left little scope to widen several internal roads.\nThe road-width changes are set out in a notification published in the state government's official gazette under Section 28(4).\nThe plan covers the nine villages merged into the Pune Municipal Corporation in 2017. A committee appointed by the state government heard public objections and suggestions and submitted its report; the revised plan is now awaiting final approval.","i":"illustration-ac3a8fe515","a":["Undri"]},{"u":"pune/pmc-to-build-multi-level-parking-near-yerawada-metro.html","h":"PMC to build multi-level parking near Yerawada Metro after Bombay High Court directions","s":"Meant particularly for commuters travelling to work and senior citizens, the facility is expected to reduce illegal roadside parking.","k":"Yerawada Metro","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-10T12:09:56+05:30","g":["Pune","Yerawada Metro","PMC","Parking","Bombay High Court"],"b":"Near Yerawada Metro Station, the Pune Municipal Corporation (PMC) is to build a multi-level parking facility on an open plot reserved for the Pune Mahanagar Parivahan Mahamandal Limited (PMPML).\nThe PMC has decided on the project and prepared a layout plan to turn the plot into a dedicated parking facility.\nThe decision follows directions from the Bombay High Court, which asked Maha Metro to take necessary steps to address congestion and parking issues around metro stations. It comes after years of complaints and follow-up by citizens.\nThe facility will take two-wheelers, three-wheelers and four-wheelers. It is meant particularly for commuters travelling to work and senior citizens who now find it hard to reach the station.\nThe project is also expected to reduce illegal roadside parking, ease traffic congestion and improve pedestrian movement around the station.\nWork on the facility is expected to begin soon.","i":"illustration-53a940bdd1","a":["Yerawada","Yerwada","Yeravda","Yerawda","Yerwda"]},{"u":"pune/hinjewadi-shivajinagar-metro-line-3-roads-remain-damaged.html","h":"Hinjewadi-Shivajinagar Metro Line 3 starts running, but roads along its route remain damaged","s":"The concessionaire has been told by the Metropolitan Commissioner to finish the pending repairs urgently.","k":"Pune Metro Line 3","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-10T11:44:58+05:30","g":["Pune Metro","Hinjewadi","Baner","PMRDA"],"b":"Roads in Baner, Balewadi, Hinjewadi and surrounding stretches are in poor condition after prolonged construction work, even as Pune Metro Line 3 between Hinjewadi and Shivajinagar has started running.\nCommuters continue to face damaged roads, potholes and uneven stretches along several parts of the route. Motorists have complained about potholes, loose concrete, uneven surfaces and damaged sections near metro stations, creating inconvenience and safety concerns.\nThe Metropolitan Commissioner has directed the concessionaire to urgently complete pending road repairs. According to PMRDA, potholes have been filled and damaged road sections are being repaired at several locations.\nCommuters are demanding proper restoration of the affected roads rather than temporary repairs, particularly on stretches with heavy daily traffic.","i":"","a":["Hinjawadi","Hinjewadi","Hinjwadi","Hinjawadi Phase 1","Hinjawadi Phase 2","Hinjawadi Phase 3","Hinjewadi Phase 1","Hinjewadi Phase 2","Hinjewadi Phase 3","Baner"]},{"u":"pune/sunil-tatkare-says-he-will-send-ramdas-kadam-legal-notice-over-allegations.html","h":"NCP MP Sunil Tatkare says he will send Ramdas Kadam legal notice over allegations after Ajit Pawar's death","s":"Sunil Tatkare called the allegations false and said Kadam should clarify allegations made against him by Anil Parab of the Thackeray faction.","k":"Tatkare and Kadam","c":"Politics","t":"2026-11-10T11:32:04+05:30","g":["Sunil Tatkare","Ramdas Kadam","Ajit Pawar","NCP"],"b":"Shiv Sena (Shinde faction) leader Ramdas Kadam demanded an inquiry into NCP MP Sunil Tatkare over alleged foul play in Deputy Chief Minister Ajit Pawar's death in a plane crash. Tatkare says he will send Kadam a legal notice over his allegations.\n‘Will send legal notice’\nTatkare\nTatkare called the allegations false and strongly condemned them. He said Kadam's mental state was not well, and jibed that Kadam should seek treatment in Agra instead of Thane.\nKadam had also alleged that Tatkare was Antulay's PA and had finished Antulay off. Tatkare denied this, saying he was never Antulay's PA and that Antulay loved him like a son.\nHe said Kadam had no moral right to speak on Antulay's leadership and that he would send Kadam a legal notice in the matter.\nInstead of accusing him, Tatkare said, Kadam should clarify the allegations that Thackeray faction leader Anil Parab has made against him.","i":"","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pune-pmc-bans-former-deputy-mayor-mukari-algude-over-molestation-allegations.html","h":"Pune: PMC bans former Deputy Mayor Mukari Algude from headquarters over molestation allegations","s":"The matter was taken to the civic body's internal complaints committee.","k":"PMC","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-10T11:19:19+05:30","g":["PMC","Mukari Algude","Vishakha Committee","Pune"],"b":"A woman employee has accused former Deputy Mayor Mukari Algude of molestation and inappropriate conduct over an incident she alleges happened on Thursday afternoon, and the Pune Municipal Corporation (PMC) has barred him from entering its headquarters.\nShe alleges that Algude entered the Social Welfare Department at the PMC main building and made inappropriate remarks towards her. She further alleges that when she objected, he grabbed her hand and pushed her away.\nShe reported the incident to senior officials, and the matter was taken to the Vishakha Committee, the civic body's internal complaints committee. Municipal employees have demanded strict action, accountability and workplace safety.\nPMC officials have confirmed that the allegations are being examined. The civic administration has restricted Algude's entry into the headquarters pending further proceedings.","i":"illustration-be8e24d5b5","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pmpml-plans-11-new-feeder-routes-pune-metro-line-3-stations.html","h":"PMPML plans 11 new feeder routes to connect Pune Metro Line 3 stations","s":"The proposed services involve 25 buses and 620 daily trips, and residents have urged PMPML to make all 11 operational at the earliest.","k":"Metro feeder routes","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-10T10:58:45+05:30","g":["PMPML","Pune Metro Line 3","Hinjewadi","feeder routes"],"b":"The Pune Mahanagar Parivahan Mahamandal Limited (PMPML) plans to introduce 11 new feeder routes linking Pune Metro Line 3 stations with nearby areas.\nPune Metro Line 3 connects Hinjewadi with Wakad, Balewadi, Baner and nearby areas, and its commuters are set to get better last-mile connectivity.\nThe proposed services will run with 25 buses and 620 trips daily, joining metro stations to nearby residential areas, IT parks, educational institutions and commercial hubs.\nThe planned routes will cover areas including Wakad, Baner, Balewadi, Hinjewadi, Wakad Chowk, Wipro Circle, Chhatrapati Shivaji Maharaj Chowk, Mitcon, Savitribai Phule Pune University and Shivajinagar Metro Station.\nThe initiative aims to encourage commuters to use public transport for daily travel, reduce dependence on private vehicles and improve access to Metro Line 3.\nResidents have urged PMPML to make all 11 services operational at the earliest and to run the buses on a regular schedule.","i":"illustration-09619625b6","a":["Hinjawadi","Hinjewadi","Hinjwadi","Hinjawadi Phase 1","Hinjawadi Phase 2","Hinjawadi Phase 3","Hinjewadi Phase 1","Hinjewadi Phase 2","Hinjewadi Phase 3"]},{"u":"pune/pune-pmpml-plans-driver-third-eye-monitoring-system-for-1000-new-buses.html","h":"Pune: PMPML plans driver ‘third eye’ monitoring system for 1,000 new buses","s":"The aim is to stop accidents that PMP bus drivers' negligence causes during journeys.","k":"PMPML","c":"City","t":"2026-11-10T10:38:50+05:30","g":["PMPML","PMP bus drivers","Pune"],"b":"The PMPML administration plans a driver monitoring system for 1,000 buses in Pune, putting PMP bus drivers under a ‘third eye’.\nThese are the 1,000 new buses that will join the PMPML fleet in the coming period.\nThe step is meant to prevent accidents caused by the negligence of PMP bus drivers during journeys.","i":"illustration-d956b706a8","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pune-airport-drop-off-pick-up-15-minute-limit-fine.html","h":"Pune airport drop-off, pick-up: 15-minute limit or ₹500 fine","s":"The fine is ₹500 for vehicles that break the rule.","k":"Pune airport","c":"City","t":"2026-11-10T10:24:34+05:30","g":["Pune airport","drop-off","pick-up","fine"],"b":"From December, vehicles entering the Pune airport premises to drop or pick up passengers will have to leave within 15 minutes.\nThose that break the rule will pay a fine of ₹500.","i":"illustration-35974d2a77","a":[]},{"u":"pune/ravet-site-construction-worker-46-falls-to-death-from-fifth-floor.html","h":"Ravet site: construction worker, 46, falls to death from fifth floor","s":"The fall on November 5 killed the construction worker, who was 46.","k":"Ravet","c":"Accidents and fires","t":"2026-11-10T10:11:42+05:30","g":["Ravet","construction worker","Pune"],"b":"A construction worker, 46, died after falling from the fifth floor of a building under construction at Ravet on November 5.","i":"illustration-581dd74f02","a":["Ravet"]},{"u":"pune/dighi-police-book-six-men-allegedly-assaulting-man-spitting-dispute.html","h":"Dighi police book six men for allegedly assaulting man in spitting dispute","s":"Dighi police have booked six men over an alleged assault that followed a row about spitting.","k":"Dighi police","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-10T09:58:47+05:30","g":["Dighi police","Spitting dispute","Pune"],"b":"Six men allegedly assaulted a man after a dispute over spitting on a public road, and Dighi police registered a case against them on Sunday.","i":"illustration-b3437aed0c","a":["Dighi"]},{"u":"pune/maharashtra-hospitals-without-fire-nocs-two-months-after-amravati-fire.html","h":"Maharashtra: 134 hospitals still without fire NOCs two months after Amravati hospital fire","s":"Fire safety audits are complete in 511 of 527 facilities, and 16 are yet to be inspected.","k":"Maharashtra","c":"Accidents and fires","t":"2026-11-10T09:46:04+05:30","g":["Maharashtra","fire safety","hospitals","Amravati"],"b":"134 hospitals across Maharashtra are still without fire NOCs, two months after the fire at the Amravati hospital.\nOf the 527 facilities, 511 have completed fire safety audits, leaving 16 yet to undergo inspections.","i":"illustration-07d7f1f83f","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pmc-takes-no-action-on-firecracker-violations-despite-diwali-ban-public-spaces.html","h":"PMC takes no action on firecracker violations despite Diwali ban in public spaces","s":"The Pune Municipal Corporation prohibited the bursting of firecrackers in public spaces during Diwali.","k":"PMC","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-10T09:33:01+05:30","g":["PMC","Diwali","firecrackers","Pune"],"b":"The Pune Municipal Corporation (PMC), which banned firecrackers in public spaces for Diwali, has taken no action against violations this year.","i":"illustration-c9f3b05a95","a":[]},{"u":"pune/khadakwasla-dams-stop-rural-water-release-by-weekend.html","h":"Khadakwasla dams to stop rural water release by weekend, leaving around 21.5 TMC","s":"Authorities are to take a call on Pune's water supply, and the dams hold around 5.5 TMC less than the storage recorded around mid-November last year.","k":"Khadakwasla dams","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-10T09:19:58+05:30","g":["Khadakwasla","Pune water supply","Rural water release"],"b":"Around 21.5 TMC of water will remain in the four dams to meet the requirements of Pune city and rural areas over the next nine months, once the Khadakwasla circle dams stop releasing water for rural areas by this weekend.\nThe existing stock is around 5.5 TMC lower than the storage recorded in the dams around mid-November last year.\nAuthorities are to take a call on Pune's water supply.","i":"illustration-416ae4ce96","a":["Khadakwasla","Khadakvasla"]},{"u":"pune/maharashtra-fda-suspends-105-food-licences-zepto-blinkit-biryani-by-kilo.html","h":"Maharashtra FDA suspends 105 food licences; Zepto, Blinkit, Biryani By Kilo under scanner","s":"The crackdown, ahead of Diwali, also saw officials seize 39,485 kg of food products worth approximately ₹1.35 crore.","k":"Maharashtra FDA","c":"Business","t":"2026-11-10T00:08:55+05:30","g":["Maharashtra FDA","Food safety","Zepto","Blinkit","Biryani By Kilo"],"b":"Following inspections on November 4 and 5, the Maharashtra Food and Drug Administration (FDA) has suspended the licences of 105 food businesses, and ordered seven establishments across Maharashtra to shut operations after detecting food safety violations.\nThis is a statewide food safety crackdown ahead of Diwali.\nZepto, Blinkit and Biryani By Kilo are among the well-known names under the FDA’s scanner.\nDuring the drive, officials seized 39,485 kg of food products worth approximately ₹1.35 crore. Violations included unhygienic storage conditions, improper food handling, inadequate pest control and lack of temperature-control facilities.","i":"illustration-df7522054e","a":[]},{"u":"pune/parth-pawar-visits-sharad-pawar-silver-oak-again-ncp-merger-talk.html","h":"Parth Pawar visits Sharad Pawar at Silver Oak again, fuelling NCP merger talk","s":"Parth Pawar went to Silver Oak, Sharad Pawar’s residence, on Saturday and again on Sunday, amid talk of whether the two NCP factions will merge.","k":"NCP merger talk","c":"Politics","t":"2026-11-08T15:53:01+05:30","g":["Parth Pawar","Sharad Pawar","NCP","Silver Oak"],"b":"On Sunday, a second day running, Parth Pawar visited Sharad Pawar at Silver Oak, fuelling talk of an NCP merger.\nSharad Pawar was sent home from Mumbai’s Breach Candy Hospital on Saturday and went to Silver Oak, his residence. Parth Pawar went there that day, amid talk of whether the proposal to merge the two NCP factions will materialise.\nAs per information received, when Parth Pawar arrived, Sharad Pawar was meeting NCP (SP) state president Shashikant Shinde, former home minister Anil Deshmukh and Jitendra Awhad. Information has emerged that Parth Pawar left after a full hour and a half. Which of the two visits this was is not clear. Shinde and Awhad have kept silent on the merger.\nSharad Pawar had sought treatment at Pune’s Ruby Hall Clinic for cough-related complications, and was admitted to Breach Candy on 4 November for further evaluations, hours after his discharge in Pune.","i":"","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pune-constable-allegedly-rams-commissioner-amitesh-kumar-gate-attempted-murder.html","h":"Pune constable allegedly rams car into Commissioner Amitesh Kumar’s gate, booked for attempted murder","s":"A Pune city police constable allegedly tried to force his way into the Police Commissioner’s residence with his car, and the city police said he has been booked for attempted murder.","k":"Pune police","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-04T16:46:04+05:30","g":["Amitesh Kumar","Amol Bhise","Pune city police","attempted murder"],"b":"A Pune city police constable allegedly rammed his car into the main gate of Police Commissioner Amitesh Kumar’s official residence on Tuesday evening, 3 November, in an attempt to force his way in, the city police said.\nThe city police said Amol Bhise, 42, has been booked for attempted murder as he allegedly tried to run over the security personnel on duty, who had stopped him from going further into the premises.\nAn officer from the Koregaon Park police station said: “There were guards on duty, whom he tried to run over. They had stopped him from going further into the premises.”\nConfirming the incident, Police Commissioner Amitesh Kumar said the constable was likely inebriated and in an unstable state of mind, and had been suspended in 2025 and reinstated in 2026.\n“He rammed into the gate and tried to enter the premises”\nPolice Commissioner Amitesh Kumar said\nPolice took Bhise into custody after the incident. Whether he has since been formally arrested or only detained is not yet clear.\nWhy he did it has not been established. Senior officials said they were looking into the reasons he tried to enter the premises.","i":"","a":[]},{"u":"pune/infratech-owner-kisan-dhavji-rathod-12-others-booked-51-buyers-allegedly-cheated.html","h":"Infratech owner Kisan Dhavji Rathod, 12 others booked: 51 buyers allegedly cheated of ₹89.07 lakh","s":"All 13 are accused of luring 51 people with low-priced flats and open plots and taking ₹89.07 lakh from them.","k":"Katraj Valley","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-04T12:02:44+05:30","g":["Infratech","Kisan Dhavji Rathod","Bharati Vidyapeeth police","Katraj Valley","cheating case"],"b":"Infratech owner Kisan Dhavji Rathod and 12 others have been booked by Bharati Vidyapeeth police in a cheating case over flats and open plots offered at low prices in a ‘Katraj Valley’ housing project; police say 51 people allegedly lost ₹89,07,000.\nPolice say the company allegedly collected booking amounts but never handed over possession.\nThe complainant is a 38-year-old nurse. Police said that in July 2023 she saw a social media advertisement for the project promising flats at affordable rates.\nAt the company’s Mangadewadi office she booked flats priced at ₹8 lakh and ₹14 lakh, and paid ₹2 lakh upfront.\nShe was allegedly told the groundbreaking would follow in six months. Six months on, she says, no work had begun.\nShe alleges she was refused a refund, and that the remaining staff told her:\n“We have not taken your money; do whatever you want.”\nthe remaining staff, she alleges\nOne buyer says not even basic excavation has been done. Other buyers say they were promised work would start around Dussehra, and that nearly ten of the company’s offices in Pune have shut.\nPolice Sub-Inspector Patil is investigating.","i":"illustration-079c16d58f","a":["Katraj Valley"]}]});window.__pvIdx&&window.__pvIdx();
